WEBVTT

00:02:44.212 --> 00:02:46.942
<i>The hills are alive</i>

00:02:47.249 --> 00:02:51.618
<i>With the sound of music</i>

00:02:51.887 --> 00:02:54.321
<i>With songs they have sung</i>

00:02:54.623 --> 00:02:59.458
<i>For a thousand years</i>

00:02:59.728 --> 00:03:02.891
<i>The hills fill my heart</i>

00:03:03.131 --> 00:03:07.659
<i>With the sound of music</i>

00:03:07.936 --> 00:03:15.104
<i>My heart wants to sing</i>
<i>Every song it hears</i>

00:03:15.610 --> 00:03:20.479
<i>My heart wants to beat like the wings</i>
<i>Of the birds that rise</i>

00:03:20.749 --> 00:03:23.809
<i>From the lake to the trees</i>

00:03:24.019 --> 00:03:28.319
<i>My heart wants to sigh</i>
<i>Like a chime that flies</i>

00:03:28.590 --> 00:03:32.526
<i>From a church on a breeze</i>

00:03:32.794 --> 00:03:36.286
<i>To laugh like a brook</i>
<i>When it trips and falls</i>

00:03:36.531 --> 00:03:40.023
<i>Over stones on its way</i>

00:03:40.302 --> 00:03:44.170
<i>To sing through the night</i>

00:03:44.439 --> 00:03:48.205
<i>Like a lark who is learning to pray</i>

00:03:48.543 --> 00:03:54.175
<i>I go to the hills</i>

00:03:54.382 --> 00:04:00.548
<i>When my heart is lonely</i>

00:04:00.822 --> 00:04:04.690
<i>I know I will hear</i>

00:04:04.893 --> 00:04:09.387
<i>What I've heard before</i>

00:04:09.664 --> 00:04:14.397
<i>My heart will be blessed</i>

00:04:14.636 --> 00:04:22.407
<i>With the sound of music</i>

00:04:23.478 --> 00:04:28.643
<i>And I'll sing...</i>

00:04:28.850 --> 00:04:37.815
<i>...once more</i>

00:09:19.874 --> 00:09:24.834
<i>Hallelujah, hallelujah</i>

00:09:25.113 --> 00:09:29.777
<i>Hallelujah, hallelujah</i>

00:09:31.986 --> 00:09:34.045
- Reverend Mother.
- Sister Bernice.

00:09:34.289 --> 00:09:36.917
- I simply cannot find her.
- Maria?

00:09:37.992 --> 00:09:39.289
She's missing again.

00:09:40.228 --> 00:09:42.594
We should've put a cowbell
around her neck.

00:09:42.831 --> 00:09:45.891
Have you tried the barn? You know
how much she adores the animals.

00:09:46.167 --> 00:09:48.897
I have looked everywhere.
In all of the usual places.

00:09:49.103 --> 00:09:51.333
Sister, considering it's Maria...

00:09:51.639 --> 00:09:54.233
...I suggest you look in someplace
unusual.

00:09:59.514 --> 00:10:00.811
Well, Reverend Mother...

00:10:01.082 --> 00:10:03.642
...I hope this new infraction ends
whatever doubts...

00:10:03.918 --> 00:10:07.149
...you may still have
about Maria's future here.

00:10:07.355 --> 00:10:11.416
I always try to keep faith
in my doubts, Sister Berthe.

00:10:11.659 --> 00:10:14.526
After all, the wool of a black sheep
is just as warm.

00:10:14.762 --> 00:10:19.096
We are not talking about sheep,
black or white, Sister Margaretta.

00:10:19.334 --> 00:10:22.770
Of all the candidates for
the novitiate, Maria is the least...

00:10:23.037 --> 00:10:25.528
Children, children.

00:10:26.007 --> 00:10:29.966
We were speculating about
the qualifications of our postulants.

00:10:30.612 --> 00:10:33.604
The Mistress of Novices
and the Mistress of Postulants...

00:10:33.848 --> 00:10:39.150
...were trying to help me
by expressing opposite points of view.

00:10:39.387 --> 00:10:42.447
Tell me, Sister Catherine,
what do you think of Maria?

00:10:42.657 --> 00:10:45.717
She's a wonderful girl,
some of the time.

00:10:46.694 --> 00:10:49.788
- Sister Agatha?
- It's very easy to like Maria...

00:10:50.031 --> 00:10:52.556
...except when it's difficult.

00:10:52.867 --> 00:10:56.428
- And you, Sister Sophia?
- Oh, I love her very dearly.

00:10:56.638 --> 00:10:59.573
But she always seems to be
in trouble, doesn't she?

00:10:59.807 --> 00:11:01.399
Exactly what I say.

00:11:01.876 --> 00:11:04.344
<i>She climbs a tree and scrapes her knee</i>

00:11:04.546 --> 00:11:06.241
<i>Her dress has got a tear</i>

00:11:06.915 --> 00:11:11.079
<i>She waltzes on her way to Mass</i>
<i>And whistles on the stair</i>

00:11:11.719 --> 00:11:16.213
<i>And underneath her wimple</i>
<i>She has curlers in her hair</i>

00:11:16.491 --> 00:11:21.087
<i>I've even heard her singing</i>
<i>In the abbey</i>

00:11:21.329 --> 00:11:23.320
<i>She's always late for chapel</i>

00:11:23.565 --> 00:11:25.829
<i>But her penitence is real</i>

00:11:26.100 --> 00:11:28.432
<i>She's always late for everything</i>

00:11:28.670 --> 00:11:30.695
<i>Except for every meal</i>

00:11:31.072 --> 00:11:35.771
<i>I hate to have to say it</i>
<i>But I very firmly feel</i>

00:11:36.010 --> 00:11:40.447
<i>Maria's not an asset to the abbey</i>

00:11:40.949 --> 00:11:43.440
<i>I'd like to say a word in her behalf</i>

00:11:43.718 --> 00:11:45.049
Say it, Sister Margaretta.

00:11:45.920 --> 00:11:49.879
<i>Maria makes me laugh</i>

00:11:52.760 --> 00:11:56.696
<i>How do you solve a problem like Maria?</i>

00:11:56.965 --> 00:12:00.765
<i>How do you catch a cloud</i>
<i>And pin it down?</i>

00:12:01.069 --> 00:12:04.402
<i>How do you find a word</i>
<i>That means Maria?</i>

00:12:04.939 --> 00:12:06.031
<i>A flibbertigibbet</i>

00:12:06.274 --> 00:12:07.605
<i>- A will-o'-the-wisp</i>
<i>- A clown</i>

00:12:09.243 --> 00:12:12.974
<i>Many a thing you know</i>
<i>You'd like to tell her</i>

00:12:13.247 --> 00:12:16.705
<i>Many a thing she ought to understand</i>

00:12:17.118 --> 00:12:20.815
<i>But how do you make her stay</i>
<i>And listen to all you say?</i>

00:12:21.389 --> 00:12:24.881
<i>How do you keep a wave upon the sand?</i>

00:12:25.126 --> 00:12:29.222
<i>How do you solve a problem like Maria?</i>

00:12:29.731 --> 00:12:35.260
<i>How do you hold a moonbeam...</i>

00:12:35.470 --> 00:12:40.931
<i>...in your hand?</i>

00:12:42.010 --> 00:12:45.502
<i>When I'm with her I'm confused</i>
<i>Out of focus and bemused</i>

00:12:45.813 --> 00:12:49.249
<i>And I never know exactly where I am</i>

00:12:49.450 --> 00:12:52.783
<i>- Unpredictable as weather</i>
<i>- She's as flighty as a feather</i>

00:12:53.154 --> 00:12:54.985
<i>- She's a darling</i>
<i>- She's a demon</i>

00:12:55.189 --> 00:12:56.520
<i>She's a lamb</i>

00:12:56.924 --> 00:13:00.587
<i>She'll out pester any pest</i>
<i>Drive a hornet from its nest</i>

00:13:00.795 --> 00:13:04.094
<i>She can throw a whirling dervish</i>
<i>Out of whirl</i>

00:13:04.666 --> 00:13:08.193
<i>- She is gentle, she is wild</i>
<i>- She's a riddle, she's a child</i>

00:13:08.770 --> 00:13:11.330
<i>- She's a headache</i>
<i>- She's an angel</i>

00:13:11.539 --> 00:13:15.441
<i>She's a girl</i>

00:13:16.177 --> 00:13:20.113
<i>How do you solve a problem like Maria?</i>

00:13:20.348 --> 00:13:24.045
<i>How do you catch a cloud</i>
<i>And pin it down?</i>

00:13:24.352 --> 00:13:27.844
<i>How do you find a word</i>
<i>That means Maria?</i>

00:13:28.122 --> 00:13:30.113
<i>- A flibbertigibbet</i>
<i>- A will-o'-the-wisp</i>

00:13:30.358 --> 00:13:31.985
<i>A clown</i>

00:13:32.460 --> 00:13:36.191
<i>Many a thing you know</i>
<i>You'd like to tell her</i>

00:13:36.464 --> 00:13:39.956
<i>Many a thing she ought to understand</i>

00:13:40.168 --> 00:13:44.502
<i>- But how do you make her stay</i>
<i>- And listen to all you say?</i>

00:13:44.739 --> 00:13:48.835
<i>How do you keep a wave upon the sand?</i>

00:13:49.043 --> 00:13:54.879
<i>How do you solve a problem like Maria?</i>

00:14:10.832 --> 00:14:17.601
<i>How do you hold a moonbeam...</i>

00:14:18.506 --> 00:14:24.911
<i>...in your hand?</i>

00:14:36.724 --> 00:14:38.715
You may go in now, Maria.

00:14:51.305 --> 00:14:52.932
Come here, my child.

00:14:59.447 --> 00:15:00.812
Now sit down.

00:15:01.749 --> 00:15:05.310
Reverend Mother, I'm sorry.
I couldn't help myself.

00:15:05.586 --> 00:15:08.555
- The hills were beckoning and before...
- Dear.

00:15:08.956 --> 00:15:10.924
I haven't summoned you for apologies.

00:15:11.159 --> 00:15:13.389
Please let me ask for forgiveness.

00:15:14.061 --> 00:15:15.289
If you'll feel better.

00:15:16.230 --> 00:15:18.596
Yes, you see,
the sky was so blue today...

00:15:18.833 --> 00:15:22.633
...and everything was so green and
fragrant, I had to be a part of it.

00:15:22.904 --> 00:15:27.398
The Untersberg led me higher like
it wanted me to go through the clouds.

00:15:27.608 --> 00:15:29.633
Suppose darkness had come
and you were lost?

00:15:29.911 --> 00:15:32.141
Mother, I could never be lost
up there.

00:15:32.413 --> 00:15:35.246
That's my mountain.
I was brought up on it.

00:15:35.449 --> 00:15:37.747
It was the mountain that led me
to you.

00:15:38.519 --> 00:15:41.488
When I was a child,
I would come down and climb a tree...

00:15:41.756 --> 00:15:43.519
...and look in your garden.

00:15:43.758 --> 00:15:46.693
I'd see the sisters at work
and hear them sing.

00:15:48.029 --> 00:15:51.658
Which brings me to another
transgression, Reverend Mother.

00:15:51.866 --> 00:15:54.027
I was singing out there today.

00:15:54.702 --> 00:15:58.729
Only in the abbey do we have rules
about postulants singing.

00:15:58.940 --> 00:16:00.965
I can't stop wherever I am.

00:16:01.175 --> 00:16:03.507
Worse, I can't seem to stop
saying things.

00:16:03.778 --> 00:16:06.042
Everything I think and feel.

00:16:06.280 --> 00:16:07.713
Some call that "honesty."

00:16:07.982 --> 00:16:10.348
Oh, but it's terrible,
Reverend Mother!

00:16:10.551 --> 00:16:14.453
You know how Sister Berthe makes me
kiss the floor after a disagreement?

00:16:14.822 --> 00:16:18.314
Lately, I kiss the floor
when I see her coming to save time.

00:16:20.995 --> 00:16:22.155
Maria...

00:16:23.164 --> 00:16:26.156
...when you saw us over the wall
and longed to be with us...

00:16:26.400 --> 00:16:31.133
...that didn't mean you were prepared
for the way we live here, did it?

00:16:32.473 --> 00:16:34.873
No, Mother, but I pray and I try.

00:16:35.076 --> 00:16:36.805
And I am learning. I really am.

00:16:37.044 --> 00:16:39.706
What is the most important lesson
you have learned here?

00:16:40.381 --> 00:16:44.181
To find out what is the will of God
and do it wholeheartedly.

00:16:47.021 --> 00:16:48.147
Maria...

00:16:49.657 --> 00:16:52.421
...it seems to be God's will
that you leave us.

00:16:52.693 --> 00:16:54.183
- Leave?
- Only for a while.

00:16:54.695 --> 00:16:57.027
No, Mother!
Please don't send me away!

00:16:57.265 --> 00:17:01.531
This is where I belong. It's my home,
my family. It's my life.

00:17:02.203 --> 00:17:05.229
- Are you truly ready for it?
- Yes, I am.

00:17:05.439 --> 00:17:10.342
If you go out into the world for a
time, knowing what we expect of you...

00:17:10.611 --> 00:17:13.341
...you will find out
if you can expect it of yourself.

00:17:13.547 --> 00:17:17.847
I know what you expect, Mother,
and I can do it! I promise I can!

00:17:21.389 --> 00:17:22.617
Yes, Mother.

00:17:24.725 --> 00:17:26.386
If it is God's will.

00:17:28.629 --> 00:17:33.760
There is a family near Salzburg that
needs a governess until September.

00:17:33.968 --> 00:17:36.198
- September?
- For seven children.

00:17:36.871 --> 00:17:37.860
Seven children?!

00:17:38.105 --> 00:17:39.367
Do you like children?

00:17:40.141 --> 00:17:41.972
Well, yes, but seven!

00:17:43.110 --> 00:17:46.273
I will tell Captain von Trapp
to expect you tomorrow.

00:17:46.814 --> 00:17:48.213
Captain?

00:17:48.916 --> 00:17:53.751
A retired officer of the Imperial
Navy. A fine man and a brave one.

00:17:53.988 --> 00:17:56.718
His wife died,
and he is alone with the children.

00:17:56.924 --> 00:18:01.224
I understand he has had a difficult
time keeping a governess there.

00:18:01.996 --> 00:18:04.294
Why difficult, Reverend Mother?

00:18:05.666 --> 00:18:08.601
The Lord will show you
in His own good time.

00:18:45.473 --> 00:18:47.941
When the Lord closes a door...

00:18:48.142 --> 00:18:50.667
...somewhere He opens a window.

00:18:53.014 --> 00:18:58.008
<i>What will this day be like?</i>

00:18:58.219 --> 00:19:00.449
<i>I wonder</i>

00:19:06.961 --> 00:19:11.057
<i>What will my future be?</i>

00:19:11.899 --> 00:19:14.163
<i>I wonder</i>

00:19:15.736 --> 00:19:18.830
<i>It could be so exciting</i>

00:19:19.040 --> 00:19:22.134
<i>To be out in the world</i>
<i>To be free</i>

00:19:22.343 --> 00:19:25.403
<i>My heart should be wildly rejoicing</i>

00:19:26.580 --> 00:19:31.916
<i>Oh, what's the matter with me?</i>

00:19:32.253 --> 00:19:35.313
<i>I've always longed for adventure</i>

00:19:35.589 --> 00:19:39.150
<i>To do the things I've never dared</i>

00:19:39.393 --> 00:19:42.590
<i>Now here I'm facing adventure</i>

00:19:42.897 --> 00:19:48.995
<i>Then why am I so scared?</i>

00:19:52.440 --> 00:19:55.341
<i>A captain with seven children</i>

00:19:55.576 --> 00:19:58.409
<i>What's so fearsome about that?</i>

00:20:00.948 --> 00:20:03.576
<i>I must stop these doubts and worries</i>

00:20:03.851 --> 00:20:06.684
<i>If I don't I just know I'll turn back</i>

00:20:06.954 --> 00:20:10.117
<i>I must dream of the things</i>
<i>I am seeking</i>

00:20:11.192 --> 00:20:16.186
<i>I am seeking the courage I lack</i>

00:20:17.098 --> 00:20:20.932
<i>The courage to serve them</i>
<i>With reliance</i>

00:20:21.202 --> 00:20:24.103
<i>Face my mistakes without defiance</i>

00:20:24.371 --> 00:20:26.066
<i>Show them I'm worthy</i>

00:20:26.307 --> 00:20:28.969
<i>And while I show them</i>

00:20:29.243 --> 00:20:33.043
<i>I'll show me</i>

00:20:33.247 --> 00:20:38.651
<i>So let them bring on</i>
<i>All their problems</i>

00:20:38.886 --> 00:20:42.151
<i>I'll do better than my best</i>

00:20:42.423 --> 00:20:45.483
<i>I have confidence</i>
<i>They'll put me to the test</i>

00:20:45.726 --> 00:20:49.162
<i>But I'll make them see</i>
<i>I have confidence in me</i>

00:20:49.396 --> 00:20:52.661
<i>Somehow I will impress them</i>

00:20:52.933 --> 00:20:56.164
<i>I will be firm but kind</i>

00:20:56.437 --> 00:20:59.736
<i>And all those children</i>
<i>Heaven bless them</i>

00:20:59.974 --> 00:21:03.273
<i>They will look up to me</i>
<i>And mind me</i>

00:21:03.511 --> 00:21:06.639
<i>With each step I am more certain</i>

00:21:06.914 --> 00:21:10.179
<i>Everything will turn out fine</i>

00:21:10.417 --> 00:21:13.511
<i>I have confidence</i>
<i>The world can all be mine</i>

00:21:13.754 --> 00:21:19.192
<i>They'll have to agree</i>
<i>I have confidence in me</i>

00:21:20.761 --> 00:21:23.491
<i>I have confidence in sunshine</i>

00:21:23.764 --> 00:21:26.858
<i>I have confidence in rain</i>

00:21:27.101 --> 00:21:29.968
<i>I have confidence</i>
<i>That spring will come again</i>

00:21:30.271 --> 00:21:33.297
<i>Besides which you see</i>
<i>I have confidence in me</i>

00:21:33.607 --> 00:21:36.667
<i>Strength doesn't lie in numbers</i>

00:21:36.944 --> 00:21:39.970
<i>Strength doesn't lie in wealth</i>

00:21:40.214 --> 00:21:43.547
<i>Strength lies in nights</i>
<i>Of peaceful slumbers</i>

00:21:43.817 --> 00:21:46.684
<i>When you wake up, wake up</i>
<i>It's healthy</i>

00:21:46.987 --> 00:21:49.979
<i>All I trust I leave my heart to</i>

00:21:50.224 --> 00:21:53.125
<i>All I trust becomes my own</i>

00:21:53.327 --> 00:21:58.128
<i>I have confidence in confidence alone</i>

00:22:12.746 --> 00:22:14.373
Oh, help.

00:22:26.560 --> 00:22:33.227
<i>I have confidence in confidence alone</i>

00:22:34.034 --> 00:22:38.835
<i>Besides which you see</i>
<i>I have confidence...</i>

00:22:39.106 --> 00:22:45.909
<i>...in me</i>

00:22:52.453 --> 00:22:54.853
Hello. Here I am.

00:22:57.691 --> 00:22:59.522
I'm from the convent.
I'm the new governess, captain.

00:23:01.195 --> 00:23:04.426
And I'm the old butler, fräulein.

00:23:06.400 --> 00:23:08.197
Well, how do you do?

00:23:18.712 --> 00:23:22.773
You'll wait here, please.

00:24:49.136 --> 00:24:53.232
In future, remember certain rooms
in this house are not to be disturbed.

00:24:54.408 --> 00:24:55.875
Yes, captain, sir.

00:25:03.817 --> 00:25:09.050
- Why do you stare at me that way?
- You don't look like a sea captain.

00:25:10.257 --> 00:25:13.317
I'm afraid you don't look
very much like a governess.

00:25:14.027 --> 00:25:15.085
- Turn around.
- What?

00:25:15.429 --> 00:25:16.691
Turn.

00:25:19.867 --> 00:25:21.027
Hat off.

00:25:24.238 --> 00:25:26.866
Put on another dress
before meeting the children.

00:25:27.174 --> 00:25:28.732
But I don't have another.

00:25:29.009 --> 00:25:31.876
When we enter the abbey,
our worldly clothes go to the poor.

00:25:32.112 --> 00:25:33.374
What about this one?

00:25:33.580 --> 00:25:34.911
The poor didn't want it.

00:25:36.750 --> 00:25:40.242
There wasn't time to make a new dress.
I can make clothes.

00:25:41.522 --> 00:25:43.786
I'll see that you get some material.

00:25:44.525 --> 00:25:46.049
Today, if possible.

00:25:47.027 --> 00:25:48.790
- Now, fräulein...
- Maria.

00:25:49.029 --> 00:25:51.759
I don't know how much
the abbess told you.

00:25:52.032 --> 00:25:54.592
You are the twelfth governess...

00:25:54.802 --> 00:25:57.270
...to look after my children
since their mother died.

00:25:57.471 --> 00:25:59.701
I trust you will be an improvement
on the last one.

00:25:59.940 --> 00:26:01.771
She stayed only two hours.

00:26:03.477 --> 00:26:06.071
What's wrong with the children, sir?

00:26:07.548 --> 00:26:11.951
Nothing is wrong with the children,
only the governesses.

00:26:12.219 --> 00:26:17.156
They could not maintain discipline,
without which the house cannot be run.

00:26:18.091 --> 00:26:19.888
Drill them in their studies.

00:26:20.127 --> 00:26:23.619
I will not permit them to dream
away their summer holidays.

00:26:23.897 --> 00:26:26.593
Each afternoon,
they march, breathing deeply.

00:26:26.800 --> 00:26:28.461
Bedtime is to be strictly observed.

00:26:28.669 --> 00:26:29.636
When do they play?

00:26:29.837 --> 00:26:33.898
You will see to it that they conduct
themselves with the utmost decorum.

00:26:34.141 --> 00:26:37.076
- I am placing you in command.
- Yes, sir.

00:27:57.724 --> 00:27:58.884
Now...

00:27:59.493 --> 00:28:02.428
...this is your new governess,
Fräulein Maria.

00:28:04.097 --> 00:28:06.088
Give your name at your signal.

00:28:06.400 --> 00:28:10.598
Fräulein, listen carefully. Learn
their signals so you can call them.

00:28:11.905 --> 00:28:13.270
Liesl.

00:28:13.540 --> 00:28:15.269
Friedrich.

00:28:15.542 --> 00:28:17.066
Louisa.

00:28:17.344 --> 00:28:18.606
Kurt.

00:28:18.845 --> 00:28:19.903
Brigitta.

00:28:20.180 --> 00:28:21.408
Marta.

00:28:27.788 --> 00:28:29.119
Gretl.

00:28:33.760 --> 00:28:37.196
Now, let's see how well you listened.

00:28:37.431 --> 00:28:39.797
I won't need to whistle for them,
Reverend Captain.

00:28:40.067 --> 00:28:43.525
I mean, I'll use their names.
Such lovely names.

00:28:43.737 --> 00:28:46.900
Fräulein, this is a large house.
The grounds are extensive.

00:28:47.140 --> 00:28:49.904
And I will not have anyone shouting.

00:28:50.143 --> 00:28:51.872
You will take this, please.
Learn to use it.

00:28:52.079 --> 00:28:53.740
The children will help you.

00:28:55.782 --> 00:28:59.775
Now, when I want you,
this is what you will hear.

00:29:00.654 --> 00:29:02.451
Oh, no, sir. I'm sorry, sir!

00:29:03.323 --> 00:29:04.881
I could never answer to a whistle.

00:29:05.092 --> 00:29:07.720
Whistles are for animals,
not for children.

00:29:07.995 --> 00:29:10.054
And definitely not for me.

00:29:10.297 --> 00:29:12.925
It would be too humiliating.

00:29:13.734 --> 00:29:18.933
Fräulein, were you this much trouble
at the abbey?

00:29:19.239 --> 00:29:20.331
Oh, much more, sir.

00:29:31.451 --> 00:29:33.009
I don't know your signal.

00:29:34.488 --> 00:29:37.116
You may call me "captain."

00:29:50.037 --> 00:29:51.504
At ease.

00:29:54.307 --> 00:29:55.865
Now that there's just us...

00:29:56.143 --> 00:30:00.307
...would you please tell me all your
names again and how old you are.

00:30:00.781 --> 00:30:04.774
I'm Liesl. I'm 16 years old,
and I don't need a governess.

00:30:05.552 --> 00:30:08.612
I'm glad you told me, Liesl.
We'll just be good friends.

00:30:10.791 --> 00:30:14.557
I'm Friedrich. I'm 14.
I'm impossible.

00:30:14.861 --> 00:30:16.522
Really? Who told you that, Friedrich?

00:30:16.797 --> 00:30:20.289
Fräulein Josephine.
Four governesses ago.

00:30:20.734 --> 00:30:22.201
I'm Brigitta.

00:30:24.037 --> 00:30:28.030
You didn't tell me how old you are,
Louisa.

00:30:28.709 --> 00:30:30.973
I'm Brigitta. She's Louisa.

00:30:31.211 --> 00:30:33.975
She's 13 years old, and you're smart.

00:30:34.214 --> 00:30:37.980
I'm 10, and I think your dress
is the ugliest one I ever saw.

00:30:38.318 --> 00:30:40.946
- Brigitta, you shouldn't say that.
- Why not?

00:30:41.154 --> 00:30:43.418
- Don't you think it's ugly?
- Of course.

00:30:43.690 --> 00:30:46.386
But Fräulein Helga's was ugliest.

00:30:46.660 --> 00:30:49.254
I'm Kurt. I'm 11.
I'm incorrigible.

00:30:49.529 --> 00:30:52.657
- Congratulations.
- What's "incorrigible"?

00:30:52.899 --> 00:30:56.767
I think it means you want
to be treated like a boy.

00:30:58.939 --> 00:31:02.238
I'm Marta, and I'm going to be
seven on Tuesday.

00:31:02.509 --> 00:31:03.874
I'd like a pink parasol.

00:31:05.078 --> 00:31:06.602
Pink's my favorite color too.

00:31:09.015 --> 00:31:10.175
Yes, you're Gretl.

00:31:11.084 --> 00:31:12.779
And you're five years old?

00:31:13.220 --> 00:31:15.211
My, you're practically a lady.

00:31:17.724 --> 00:31:20.750
I have to tell you a secret.
I've never been a governess.

00:31:22.195 --> 00:31:24.959
You don't know anything
about being a governess?

00:31:25.232 --> 00:31:26.597
Nothing. I'll need lots of advice.

00:31:27.567 --> 00:31:32.095
The best way to start is to tell
Father to mind his own business.

00:31:32.305 --> 00:31:34.102
Never come to dinner on time.

00:31:34.307 --> 00:31:36.605
Never eat your soup quietly.

00:31:37.277 --> 00:31:39.370
During dessert, always blow your nose.

00:31:39.613 --> 00:31:42.411
Don't you believe a word they say,
Fräulein Maria.

00:31:42.616 --> 00:31:45.983
- Oh, why not?
- Because I like you.

00:31:46.787 --> 00:31:48.778
Children, outside for your walk.

00:31:48.989 --> 00:31:50.889
Father's orders. Hurry up.

00:31:51.091 --> 00:31:52.388
Quick, quick, quick.

00:31:52.626 --> 00:31:55.823
Fräulein Maria, I'm Frau Schmidt,
the housekeeper.

00:31:56.062 --> 00:31:57.120
How do you do.

00:31:57.330 --> 00:32:00.231
I'll show you to your room.
Follow me.

00:32:11.311 --> 00:32:13.074
Poor little dears.

00:32:25.792 --> 00:32:30.161
You're very lucky. With
Fräulein Helga it was a snake.

00:32:44.010 --> 00:32:45.341
Good evening.

00:32:46.780 --> 00:32:50.341
- Good evening, children.
- Good evening, Fräulein Maria.

00:32:57.557 --> 00:32:59.184
Enchanting little ritual.

00:32:59.392 --> 00:33:02.122
Something you learned at the abbey?

00:33:03.330 --> 00:33:05.662
No.

00:33:07.300 --> 00:33:08.562
Rheumatism.

00:33:18.378 --> 00:33:21.541
Excuse me, captain. Haven't we
forgotten to thank the Lord?

00:33:29.756 --> 00:33:32.725
For what we receive,
may the Lord make us truly thankful.

00:33:33.260 --> 00:33:35.194
- Amen.
- Amen.

00:33:39.733 --> 00:33:41.667
I'd like to thank you all...

00:33:41.868 --> 00:33:44.860
...for the precious gift
you left in my pocket today.

00:33:48.375 --> 00:33:50.172
What gift?

00:33:53.280 --> 00:33:55.441
It's a secret between
the children and me.

00:33:55.715 --> 00:33:59.344
Then I suggest you keep it,
and let us eat.

00:33:59.719 --> 00:34:01.687
Knowing how nervous
I must have been...

00:34:01.922 --> 00:34:04.356
...a stranger in a new household...

00:34:04.557 --> 00:34:07.617
...knowing how important it was
for me to feel accepted...

00:34:07.894 --> 00:34:12.092
...it was so kind and thoughtful of
you to make my first moments here...

00:34:12.365 --> 00:34:14.560
...so warm and happy...

00:34:14.768 --> 00:34:16.531
...and pleasant.

00:34:25.779 --> 00:34:27.804
- What is the matter, Marta?
- Nothing.

00:34:40.226 --> 00:34:41.250
Fräulein...

00:34:41.494 --> 00:34:45.328
...is it to be at every meal
or merely at dinnertime...

00:34:45.565 --> 00:34:50.127
...that you intend leading us through
this rare and wonderful new world...

00:34:50.337 --> 00:34:51.998
...of indigestion?

00:34:53.573 --> 00:34:56.440
They're all right, captain.
They're just happy.

00:35:15.195 --> 00:35:17.857
- Rolfe, good evening.
- Good evening, Franz.

00:35:18.131 --> 00:35:20.861
- I trust everything is under control?
- Yes, yes.

00:35:22.502 --> 00:35:24.936
- Are there any developments?
- Perhaps.

00:35:25.138 --> 00:35:27.299
- Is the captain home?
- He's at dinner.

00:35:27.540 --> 00:35:29.872
- With the family?
- Yes.

00:35:30.143 --> 00:35:31.940
Give him this telegram at once.

00:35:32.679 --> 00:35:33.771
Certainly.

00:35:45.458 --> 00:35:47.153
A telegram for you, sir.

00:35:49.996 --> 00:35:51.827
Franz? Who delivered it?

00:35:52.132 --> 00:35:54.157
That young lad Rolfe, of course.

00:35:56.503 --> 00:35:58.232
Father, may I be excused?

00:35:59.205 --> 00:36:03.665
Children, in the morning I shall
be going to Vienna.

00:36:03.977 --> 00:36:06.411
Not again, Father!

00:36:10.316 --> 00:36:12.375
How long will you be gone this time?

00:36:13.019 --> 00:36:14.486
I'm not sure, Gretl.

00:36:14.687 --> 00:36:18.248
- To visit Baroness Schraeder again?
- Mind your own business!

00:36:19.225 --> 00:36:21.159
As a matter of fact, yes, Louisa.

00:36:22.929 --> 00:36:26.763
- Why can't we ever see the baroness?
- Why would she want to see you?

00:36:27.067 --> 00:36:31.936
You are going to see the baroness.
I'm bringing her back with me to visit.

00:36:33.440 --> 00:36:35.237
And Uncle Max.

00:36:35.508 --> 00:36:37.908
Uncle Max!

00:36:53.960 --> 00:36:55.291
Rolfe!

00:36:58.364 --> 00:36:59.422
Oh, Rolfe!

00:37:01.968 --> 00:37:04.903
- No, Liesl. We mustn't!
- Why not, silly?

00:37:05.138 --> 00:37:07.800
- I don't know...
- Isn't this why you're waiting?

00:37:08.041 --> 00:37:09.906
Yes, of course.

00:37:10.110 --> 00:37:12.908
- I've missed you, Liesl.
- You have? How much?

00:37:13.146 --> 00:37:16.980
I even thought of sending a telegram,
so I'd be able to deliver it here.

00:37:17.250 --> 00:37:21.152
Oh, that's a lovely thought!
Why don't you, right now?

00:37:21.421 --> 00:37:25.585
- But I'm here!
- Please, Rolfe. Send me a telegram.

00:37:25.792 --> 00:37:29.250
I'll start it for you.
"Dear Liesl..."

00:37:29.929 --> 00:37:33.558
"Dear Liesl: I'd like to be able
to tell you...

00:37:33.800 --> 00:37:35.995
...how I feel about you. Stop.

00:37:36.236 --> 00:37:40.764
Unfortunately, this wire
is already too expensive.

00:37:40.974 --> 00:37:42.407
Sincerely, Rolfe."

00:37:42.609 --> 00:37:45.373
- "Sincerely"?
- Cordially.

00:37:45.578 --> 00:37:48.240
- "Cordially"?
- Affectionately?

00:37:50.617 --> 00:37:52.642
Will there be any reply?

00:37:53.920 --> 00:37:56.081
"Dear Rolfe: Stop.

00:37:57.090 --> 00:38:00.184
Don't stop! Your Liesl."

00:38:01.928 --> 00:38:05.762
If only we didn't have to wait
for someone to send Father a telegram.

00:38:06.032 --> 00:38:08.432
How do I know when I'll see you again?

00:38:09.335 --> 00:38:10.529
Well, let's see...

00:38:13.540 --> 00:38:15.508
I could come here by mistake.

00:38:16.509 --> 00:38:21.139
With a telegram for Colonel Schneider!
He's here from Berlin staying with...

00:38:22.048 --> 00:38:25.347
No one knows he's here.
Don't tell your father.

00:38:25.618 --> 00:38:28.781
- Why not?
- Your father's so Austrian.

00:38:28.988 --> 00:38:30.285
We're all Austrian.

00:38:30.490 --> 00:38:34.893
Some think we ought to be German, and
they're very mad at those who don't.

00:38:35.128 --> 00:38:36.891
They're getting ready to...

00:38:38.565 --> 00:38:40.999
Let's hope your father
doesn't get into trouble.

00:38:41.301 --> 00:38:46.204
Don't worry. He's a big naval hero.
He was even decorated by the emperor.

00:38:46.406 --> 00:38:49.671
I don't worry about him.
I worry about his daughter.

00:38:50.210 --> 00:38:51.677
Me? Why?

00:38:51.978 --> 00:38:53.536
- Well, you're so...
- What?

00:38:53.980 --> 00:38:55.470
You're such a baby!

00:38:55.915 --> 00:38:58.816
I'm 16.
What's such a baby about that?

00:39:01.054 --> 00:39:04.581
<i>You wait, little girl</i>
<i>On an empty stage</i>

00:39:04.824 --> 00:39:08.191
<i>For fate to turn the light on</i>

00:39:08.828 --> 00:39:12.059
<i>Your life, little girl</i>
<i>Is an empty page</i>

00:39:12.332 --> 00:39:16.393
<i>That men will want to write on</i>

00:39:17.103 --> 00:39:22.598
<i>To write on</i>

00:39:23.543 --> 00:39:27.479
<i>You are 16 going on 17</i>

00:39:27.680 --> 00:39:31.514
<i>Baby, it's time to think</i>

00:39:31.718 --> 00:39:35.347
<i>Better beware</i>
<i>Be canny and careful</i>

00:39:35.588 --> 00:39:39.217
<i>Baby, you're on the brink</i>

00:39:39.559 --> 00:39:43.393
<i>You are 16 going on 17</i>

00:39:43.596 --> 00:39:47.259
<i>Fellows will fall in line</i>

00:39:47.567 --> 00:39:50.900
<i>Eager young lads</i>
<i>And roués and cads</i>

00:39:51.104 --> 00:39:55.040
<i>Will offer you food and wine</i>

00:39:55.308 --> 00:39:59.074
<i>Totally unprepared are you</i>

00:39:59.479 --> 00:40:03.040
<i>To face a world of men</i>

00:40:03.616 --> 00:40:07.780
<i>Timid and shy and scared are you</i>

00:40:08.087 --> 00:40:11.579
<i>Of things beyond your ken</i>

00:40:11.791 --> 00:40:15.659
<i>You need someone older and wiser</i>

00:40:15.895 --> 00:40:19.763
<i>Telling you what to do</i>

00:40:19.999 --> 00:40:23.435
<i>I am 17 going on 18</i>

00:40:23.670 --> 00:40:29.631
<i>I'll take care of you</i>

00:41:02.175 --> 00:41:05.508
<i>I am 16 going on 17</i>

00:41:05.712 --> 00:41:09.113
<i>I know that I'm naive</i>

00:41:09.382 --> 00:41:12.613
<i>Fellows I meet</i>
<i>May tell me I'm sweet</i>

00:41:12.852 --> 00:41:16.549
<i>And willingly I believe</i>

00:41:17.023 --> 00:41:20.186
<i>I am 16 going on 17</i>

00:41:20.393 --> 00:41:24.159
<i>Innocent as a rose</i>

00:41:24.364 --> 00:41:27.822
<i>Bachelor dandies</i>
<i>Drinkers of brandies</i>

00:41:28.134 --> 00:41:31.467
<i>What do I know of those?</i>

00:41:31.671 --> 00:41:35.198
<i>Totally unprepared am I</i>

00:41:35.475 --> 00:41:38.967
<i>To face a world of men</i>

00:41:39.379 --> 00:41:42.712
<i>Timid and shy and scared am I</i>

00:41:42.982 --> 00:41:46.645
<i>Of things beyond my ken</i>

00:41:47.086 --> 00:41:50.681
<i>I need someone older and wiser</i>

00:41:50.923 --> 00:41:54.222
<i>Telling me what to do</i>

00:41:54.560 --> 00:41:58.257
<i>You are 17 going on 18</i>

00:41:58.498 --> 00:42:04.164
<i>I'll depend on you</i>

00:43:57.216 --> 00:43:58.649
Come in.

00:43:59.685 --> 00:44:01.312
Frau Schmidt.

00:44:03.656 --> 00:44:05.385
For your new dresses.

00:44:05.691 --> 00:44:09.684
- The captain had these sent from town.
- Oh, how lovely!

00:44:09.962 --> 00:44:13.398
These will make the prettiest
clothes I've ever had.

00:44:13.666 --> 00:44:17.158
Do you think he would
get me more material if I asked?

00:44:17.403 --> 00:44:21.032
- How many dresses do you need?
- Not for me, for the children.

00:44:21.307 --> 00:44:23.366
I want to make them some play clothes.

00:44:23.643 --> 00:44:27.170
The von Trapp children don't play.
They march.

00:44:27.680 --> 00:44:30.080
Surely you don't approve of that.

00:44:31.083 --> 00:44:33.483
Ever since the captain
lost his poor wife...

00:44:33.719 --> 00:44:36.415
...he runs this house as if on
one of his ships.

00:44:37.256 --> 00:44:38.655
Whistles, orders.

00:44:38.925 --> 00:44:40.756
No more music, no more laughing.

00:44:41.027 --> 00:44:44.554
Nothing that reminds him of her.
Even the children.

00:44:45.064 --> 00:44:46.156
But that's so wrong.

00:44:46.999 --> 00:44:48.523
Oh, well.

00:44:48.734 --> 00:44:52.397
How do you like your room?
There'll be new drapes at the windows.

00:44:52.672 --> 00:44:53.934
Bu these are fine.

00:44:54.173 --> 00:44:55.834
New ones have been ordered.

00:44:56.042 --> 00:44:59.341
- But I really don't need them.
- Good night, now.

00:44:59.579 --> 00:45:03.606
Frau Schmidt, if I asked
the captain about the material...?

00:45:03.883 --> 00:45:08.343
- He's leaving in the morning.
- Of course. How long will he be gone?

00:45:08.921 --> 00:45:13.517
It depends. The last time he visited
the baroness, he stayed for a month.

00:45:14.694 --> 00:45:19.256
I shouldn't be saying this to you.
I don't know you that well.

00:45:19.532 --> 00:45:22.433
But if you ask me,
the captain's thinking seriously...

00:45:22.635 --> 00:45:24.933
...of marrying her before
summer's over.

00:45:25.137 --> 00:45:28.368
Wonderful! The children will
have a mother again.

00:45:29.809 --> 00:45:31.106
Yes.

00:45:31.377 --> 00:45:33.106
Well, good night.

00:45:33.312 --> 00:45:34.745
Good night.

00:45:53.165 --> 00:45:55.998
Dear Father, now I know
why You sent me here.

00:45:56.235 --> 00:45:59.102
To help these children
prepare for a new mother.

00:45:59.338 --> 00:46:02.637
And I pray this will become
a happy family in Thy sight.

00:46:02.842 --> 00:46:05.970
God bless the captain.
God bless Liesl and Friedrich.

00:46:06.178 --> 00:46:10.342
God bless Louisa, Brigitta,
Marta and little Gretl.

00:46:10.650 --> 00:46:13.483
And I forgot the other boy.
What's his name?

00:46:15.254 --> 00:46:17.085
Well, God bless what's-his-name.

00:46:17.289 --> 00:46:21.282
God bless the Reverend Mother
and Sister Margaretta...

00:46:21.494 --> 00:46:23.291
...and everybody at the abbey.

00:46:23.496 --> 00:46:26.021
And now, dear God, about Liesl.

00:46:26.532 --> 00:46:28.432
Help her know that I'm her friend...

00:46:28.634 --> 00:46:31.194
...and help her tell me
what she's been up to.

00:46:31.937 --> 00:46:33.097
Are you going to tell on me?

00:46:33.339 --> 00:46:36.775
Help me to be understanding
so I may guide her footsteps.

00:46:37.043 --> 00:46:39.671
In the name of the Father,
the Son and the Holy Ghost.

00:46:39.879 --> 00:46:42.871
I was out walking
and somebody locked the doors early.

00:46:43.182 --> 00:46:46.811
I didn't want to wake everybody,
so when I saw your window open...

00:46:48.454 --> 00:46:51.480
You're not going to tell Father,
are you?

00:46:57.563 --> 00:46:58.860
How did you climb up?

00:46:59.365 --> 00:47:02.493
It's how we always got in
to play tricks on the governess.

00:47:02.702 --> 00:47:05.694
Louisa can make it with
a whole jar of spiders in her hand.

00:47:06.706 --> 00:47:08.367
Spiders?

00:47:12.078 --> 00:47:14.706
Were you out walking all by yourself?

00:47:22.188 --> 00:47:25.885
If we wash that dress tonight,
nobody would notice it tomorrow.

00:47:26.559 --> 00:47:28.322
You could put this on.

00:47:30.062 --> 00:47:32.758
Take your dress and put it
to soak in the bathtub.

00:47:32.998 --> 00:47:36.525
Come back here and sit on the bed,
and we'll have a talk.

00:47:37.837 --> 00:47:40.863
I told you today
I didn't need a governess.

00:47:41.073 --> 00:47:43.166
Well, maybe I do.

00:48:13.639 --> 00:48:16.199
Gretl, are you scared?

00:48:19.712 --> 00:48:21.976
You're not frightened
of a storm, are you?

00:48:22.214 --> 00:48:24.478
You just stay right here with me.

00:48:25.651 --> 00:48:29.883
- Where are the others?
- They're asleep. They're not scared.

00:48:34.293 --> 00:48:36.124
Oh, no? Look.

00:48:37.663 --> 00:48:39.631
All right, up here on the bed.

00:48:39.932 --> 00:48:42.628
- Really?
- Well, just this once. Come on.

00:48:43.736 --> 00:48:48.070
- Now we'll wait for the boys.
- You won't see them. Boys are brave.

00:48:54.146 --> 00:48:55.943
You weren't scared, were you?

00:48:56.482 --> 00:48:59.679
Oh, no. We just wanted
to be sure that you weren't.

00:49:00.786 --> 00:49:03.812
- That's very thoughtful of you.
- It wasn't my idea.

00:49:04.123 --> 00:49:05.954
It was Kurt's!

00:49:06.192 --> 00:49:08.786
Kurt! That's the one I left out!
God bless Kurt.

00:49:11.597 --> 00:49:13.360
Why does it do that?

00:49:13.599 --> 00:49:17.433
The lightning talks to the thunder,
and the thunder answers.

00:49:17.670 --> 00:49:20.161
- But lightning must be nasty.
- Not really.

00:49:20.439 --> 00:49:22.703
Why does the thunder get so angry?

00:49:22.975 --> 00:49:25.102
It makes me want to cry.

00:49:26.979 --> 00:49:31.177
Whenever I'm feeling unhappy,
I just try to think of nice things.

00:49:31.383 --> 00:49:33.214
What kind of things?

00:49:33.986 --> 00:49:35.954
Well, let me see. Nice things...

00:49:36.188 --> 00:49:37.280
Daffodils.

00:49:38.557 --> 00:49:39.956
Green meadows.

00:49:40.359 --> 00:49:42.623
Skies full of stars.

00:49:42.828 --> 00:49:46.025
<i>Raindrops on roses</i>
<i>and whiskers on kittens</i>

00:49:46.232 --> 00:49:49.360
<i>Bright copper kettles</i>
<i>And warm woolen mittens</i>

00:49:49.568 --> 00:49:52.731
<i>Brown paper packages</i>
<i>Tied up with strings</i>

00:49:53.005 --> 00:49:56.998
<i>These are a few of my favorite things</i>

00:49:59.578 --> 00:50:02.376
<i>Cream-colored ponies</i>
<i>And crisp apple strudels</i>

00:50:02.648 --> 00:50:05.845
<i>Doorbells and sleigh bells</i>
<i>And schnitzel with noodles</i>

00:50:06.085 --> 00:50:09.020
<i>Wild geese that fly</i>
<i>With the moon on their wings</i>

00:50:09.255 --> 00:50:13.089
<i>These are a few of my favorite things</i>

00:50:14.360 --> 00:50:17.090
<i>Girls in white dresses</i>
<i>With blue satin sashes</i>

00:50:17.363 --> 00:50:20.560
<i>Snowflakes that stay</i>
<i>On my nose and eyelashes</i>

00:50:20.833 --> 00:50:23.893
<i>Silver white winters</i>
<i>That melt into springs</i>

00:50:24.169 --> 00:50:27.536
<i>These are a few of my favorite things</i>

00:50:27.740 --> 00:50:29.435
<i>When the dog bites</i>

00:50:29.675 --> 00:50:31.336
<i>When the bee stings</i>

00:50:31.577 --> 00:50:33.841
<i>When I'm feeling sad</i>

00:50:34.079 --> 00:50:37.446
<i>I simply remember my favorite things</i>

00:50:37.716 --> 00:50:44.554
<i>And then I don't feel so bad</i>

00:50:45.291 --> 00:50:46.952
- Does it work?
- Of course.

00:50:47.259 --> 00:50:49.193
- What do you like?
- Pussy willow!

00:50:49.895 --> 00:50:52.125
- Christmas!
- Bunny rabbits!

00:50:52.364 --> 00:50:54.025
Snakes!

00:50:54.300 --> 00:50:56.427
- Chocolate icing!
- No school!

00:50:56.735 --> 00:50:57.861
Pillow fights!

00:50:58.137 --> 00:51:00.128
- Telegrams!
- Birthday presents!

00:51:00.539 --> 00:51:02.905
- Any presents!
- Ladybugs!

00:51:04.410 --> 00:51:05.741
A good sneeze!

00:51:06.045 --> 00:51:07.774
Gesundheit!

00:51:08.080 --> 00:51:09.308
See what fun it is?

00:51:09.548 --> 00:51:12.483
<i>Raindrops on roses</i>
<i>And whiskers on kittens</i>

00:51:12.751 --> 00:51:15.618
<i>Bright copper kettles</i>
<i>And warm woolen mittens</i>

00:51:15.888 --> 00:51:18.880
<i>Brown paper packages</i>
<i>Tied up with strings</i>

00:51:19.124 --> 00:51:21.957
<i>These are a few of my favorite things</i>

00:51:25.397 --> 00:51:28.230
<i>Cream-colored ponies</i>
<i>And crisp apple strudels</i>

00:51:28.467 --> 00:51:31.334
<i>Doorbells and sleigh bells</i>
<i>And schnitzel with noodles</i>

00:51:31.570 --> 00:51:34.505
<i>Wild geese that fly</i>
<i>With the moon on their wings</i>

00:51:34.773 --> 00:51:38.265
<i>These are a few of my favorite things</i>

00:51:39.244 --> 00:51:40.734
Together.

00:51:41.013 --> 00:51:43.777
<i>Girls in white dresses</i>
<i>With blue satin sashes</i>

00:51:44.016 --> 00:51:46.917
<i>Snowflakes that stay</i>
<i>On my nose and eyelashes</i>

00:51:47.152 --> 00:51:50.144
<i>Silver white winters</i>
<i>That melt into springs</i>

00:51:50.422 --> 00:51:53.687
<i>These are a few of my favorite things</i>

00:51:53.993 --> 00:51:56.120
<i>When the dog bi...</i>

00:51:56.328 --> 00:51:58.296
Dog bites.

00:52:04.937 --> 00:52:06.165
Hello.

00:52:06.372 --> 00:52:10.536
Fräulein, did I not tell you that
bedtime is to be strictly observed?

00:52:10.843 --> 00:52:13.539
The children were upset
by the storm, so l...

00:52:14.947 --> 00:52:15.936
You did, sir.

00:52:16.148 --> 00:52:20.346
Do you, or do you not, have difficulty
remembering such simple instructions?

00:52:21.653 --> 00:52:23.280
Only during thunderstorms.

00:52:25.791 --> 00:52:27.281
Liesl?

00:52:27.526 --> 00:52:29.721
I don't recall seeing you
after dinner.

00:52:30.329 --> 00:52:32.058
Really? As a matter of fact...

00:52:32.331 --> 00:52:33.559
Yes?

00:52:34.366 --> 00:52:35.526
Well, I was...

00:52:35.801 --> 00:52:37.860
What she would like to say...

00:52:38.070 --> 00:52:40.971
...is that she and I have
been getting acquainted tonight.

00:52:41.173 --> 00:52:46.042
It's too late to go into that. You
heard your father. Go back to bed.

00:52:50.682 --> 00:52:52.081
Fräulein...

00:52:52.384 --> 00:52:56.411
...you have managed to remember
I'm leaving in the morning?

00:52:57.523 --> 00:53:02.051
Is it also possible you remember the
first rule in this house is discipline?

00:53:03.729 --> 00:53:06.220
Then I trust that before I return...

00:53:06.732 --> 00:53:08.495
...you'll have acquired some?

00:53:09.868 --> 00:53:11.233
Captain?

00:53:12.204 --> 00:53:16.106
Could I talk to you about clothes
for the children for when they play?

00:53:16.375 --> 00:53:19.071
- If I could have some material.
- You are many things.

00:53:19.344 --> 00:53:21.505
Not the least of which is repetitious.

00:53:21.713 --> 00:53:23.874
- But they're children!
- Yes.

00:53:24.116 --> 00:53:25.879
And I'm their father.

00:53:26.452 --> 00:53:27.680
Good night.

00:53:51.944 --> 00:53:57.780
<i>Girls in white dresses</i>
<i>With blue satin sashes</i>

00:54:09.294 --> 00:54:12.821
<i>When the dog bites</i>
<i>When the bee stings</i>

00:54:13.065 --> 00:54:15.556
<i>When I'm feeling sad</i>

00:54:15.801 --> 00:54:19.100
<i>I simply remember my favorite things</i>

00:54:19.304 --> 00:54:21.431
<i>And then I don't feel...</i>

00:54:21.673 --> 00:54:28.602
<i>...so bad</i>

00:54:52.604 --> 00:54:55.300
Children, over here. See!

00:54:58.944 --> 00:55:00.309
Come on.

00:56:23.362 --> 00:56:24.590
Fräulein Maria?

00:56:24.863 --> 00:56:26.763
Can we do this every day?

00:56:27.065 --> 00:56:30.262
- Don't you think you'd get tired of it?
- I suppose so.

00:56:30.602 --> 00:56:31.864
Every other day?

00:56:32.070 --> 00:56:36.700
I haven't had so much fun since we put
glue on Fräulein Josephine's toothbrush.

00:56:36.908 --> 00:56:40.810
I can't understand how children
as nice as you can play such tricks.

00:56:41.079 --> 00:56:42.910
- It's easy.
- But why do it?

00:56:43.115 --> 00:56:45.549
How else can we get
Father's attention?

00:56:46.318 --> 00:56:47.910
Oh, I see.

00:56:49.254 --> 00:56:51.449
We'll have to think about that one.

00:56:53.625 --> 00:56:55.252
All right, over here.

00:56:55.460 --> 00:56:56.893
What are we going to do?

00:56:57.129 --> 00:56:59.097
Think of a song for the baroness.

00:56:59.331 --> 00:57:01.299
Father doesn't like us to sing.

00:57:01.566 --> 00:57:05.127
Perhaps we can change his mind.
Now, what songs do you know?

00:57:05.404 --> 00:57:07.565
We don't know any songs.

00:57:07.806 --> 00:57:10.468
- Not any?
- We don't even know how to sing.

00:57:12.144 --> 00:57:14.305
Let's not lose time. You must learn.

00:57:14.579 --> 00:57:16.308
But how?

00:57:20.619 --> 00:57:24.578
<i>Let's start at the very beginning</i>

00:57:24.790 --> 00:57:28.157
<i>A very good place to start</i>

00:57:28.360 --> 00:57:30.294
<i>When you read you begin with</i>

00:57:30.529 --> 00:57:31.757
<i>A, B, C</i>

00:57:31.963 --> 00:57:36.297
<i>When you sing, you begin with</i>
<i>Do-Re-Mi</i>

00:57:36.535 --> 00:57:38.162
<i>Do-re-mi</i>

00:57:38.437 --> 00:57:39.768
<i>Do-re-mi</i>

00:57:40.005 --> 00:57:43.839
<i>The first three notes</i>
<i>Just happen to be</i>

00:57:44.109 --> 00:57:45.872
<i>Do-re-mi</i>

00:57:46.111 --> 00:57:47.373
<i>Do-re-mi</i>

00:57:47.612 --> 00:57:51.548
<i>Do-re-mi-fa-so-la-ti</i>

00:57:52.217 --> 00:57:54.651
Let's see if I can make it easier.

00:57:58.056 --> 00:58:01.719
<i>"Doe," a deer</i>
<i>A female deer</i>

00:58:01.960 --> 00:58:05.521
<i>"Ray," a drop of golden sun</i>

00:58:05.797 --> 00:58:09.563
<i>"Me," a name I call myself</i>

00:58:09.835 --> 00:58:13.532
<i>"Far," a long long way to run</i>

00:58:13.805 --> 00:58:17.571
<i>"Sew," a needle pulling thread</i>

00:58:17.876 --> 00:58:21.710
<i>"La," a note to follow sew</i>

00:58:21.980 --> 00:58:24.915
<i>"Tea," a drink with jam and bread</i>

00:58:25.384 --> 00:58:29.480
<i>That will bring us back to doe</i>

00:58:29.988 --> 00:58:33.549
<i>- Doe</i>
<i>- A deer, a female deer</i>

00:58:33.825 --> 00:58:37.022
<i>- Ray</i>
<i>- A drop of golden sun</i>

00:58:37.262 --> 00:58:40.561
<i>- Me</i>
<i>- A name I call myself</i>

00:58:40.832 --> 00:58:43.926
<i>- Far</i>
<i>- A long long way to run</i>

00:58:44.436 --> 00:58:47.894
<i>Sew, a needle pulling thread</i>

00:58:48.106 --> 00:58:51.439
<i>- La</i>
<i>- A note to follow sew</i>

00:58:51.877 --> 00:58:54.744
<i>- Tea</i>
<i>- A drink with jam and bread</i>

00:58:55.013 --> 00:58:57.277
<i>That will bring us back to</i>

00:58:57.516 --> 00:59:00.952
<i>- Doe</i>
<i>- A deer, a female deer</i>

00:59:01.219 --> 00:59:04.279
<i>Ray, a drop of golden sun</i>

00:59:04.756 --> 00:59:07.953
<i>Me, a name I call myself</i>

00:59:08.226 --> 00:59:11.286
<i>Far, a long long way to run</i>

00:59:11.563 --> 00:59:14.794
<i>Sew, a needle pulling thread</i>

00:59:15.100 --> 00:59:18.467
<i>La, a note to follow sew</i>

00:59:18.737 --> 00:59:21.365
<i>Tea, a drink with jam and bread</i>

00:59:21.573 --> 00:59:25.634
<i>That will bring us back to doe</i>

00:59:26.044 --> 00:59:29.138
<i>Do-re-mi-fa-so-la-ti-do, so-do</i>

00:59:29.581 --> 00:59:34.143
Do-re-mi-fa-so and so on are only
the tools we use to build a song.

00:59:34.419 --> 00:59:37.650
Once you have them in your head
you can sing different tunes...

00:59:37.923 --> 00:59:40.050
...by mixing them up. Like this:

00:59:41.293 --> 00:59:46.788
<i>So-do-la-fa-mi-do-re</i>

00:59:46.998 --> 00:59:48.090
Can you do that?

00:59:48.300 --> 00:59:53.795
<i>So-do-la-fa-mi-do-re</i>

00:59:54.005 --> 00:59:59.671
<i>So-do-la-ti-do-re-do</i>

00:59:59.978 --> 01:00:05.280
<i>So-do-la-ti-do-re-do</i>

01:00:05.484 --> 01:00:07.247
Now, put it all together.

01:00:07.452 --> 01:00:14.085
<i>So-do-la-fa-mi-do-re</i>

01:00:14.326 --> 01:00:20.287
<i>So-do-la-ti-do-re-do</i>

01:00:20.866 --> 01:00:23.460
- Good.
- But it doesn't mean anything.

01:00:23.702 --> 01:00:26.671
So we put in words.
One word for every note.

01:00:26.938 --> 01:00:28.200
Like this:

01:00:28.440 --> 01:00:35.004
<i>When you know the notes to sing</i>

01:00:35.280 --> 01:00:40.877
<i>You can sing most anything</i>

01:00:41.152 --> 01:00:42.119
Together!

01:00:42.320 --> 01:00:49.021
<i>When you know the notes to sing</i>

01:00:49.227 --> 01:00:55.894
<i>You can sing most anything</i>

01:00:56.301 --> 01:00:59.668
<i>- Doe</i>
<i>- A deer, a female deer</i>

01:00:59.938 --> 01:01:03.135
<i>- Ray</i>
<i>- A drop of golden sun</i>

01:01:03.408 --> 01:01:06.639
<i>- Me</i>
<i>- A name I call myself</i>

01:01:06.845 --> 01:01:09.905
<i>- Far</i>
<i>- A long long way to run</i>

01:01:10.148 --> 01:01:13.515
<i>- Sew</i>
<i>- A needle pulling thread</i>

01:01:13.818 --> 01:01:17.083
<i>- La</i>
<i>- A note to follow sew</i>

01:01:17.289 --> 01:01:20.281
<i>- Tea</i>
<i>- A drink with jam and bread</i>

01:01:20.492 --> 01:01:24.360
<i>That will bring us back to doe</i>

01:01:41.947 --> 01:01:48.216
<i>When you know the notes to sing</i>

01:01:48.787 --> 01:01:55.283
<i>You can sing most anything</i>

01:01:55.860 --> 01:01:59.023
<i>Doe</i>
<i>A deer, a female deer</i>

01:01:59.297 --> 01:02:02.824
<i>Ray</i>
<i>A drop of golden sun</i>

01:02:03.034 --> 01:02:06.492
<i>Me</i>
<i>A name I call myself</i>

01:02:06.738 --> 01:02:09.901
<i>Far</i>
<i>A long long way to run</i>

01:02:10.175 --> 01:02:13.338
<i>Sew</i>
<i>A needle pulling thread</i>

01:02:13.545 --> 01:02:16.742
<i>La</i>
<i>A note to follow sew</i>

01:02:17.349 --> 01:02:19.977
<i>Tea</i>
<i>A drink with jam and bread</i>

01:02:20.218 --> 01:02:24.177
<i>That will bring us back to</i>

01:02:24.389 --> 01:02:31.227
<i>So-do-la-fa-mi-do-re</i>

01:02:31.496 --> 01:02:35.990
<i>So-do-la-fa-ti</i>

01:02:36.234 --> 01:02:37.861
<i>La-so</i>

01:02:41.406 --> 01:02:47.208
<i>Ti-do</i>

01:02:47.412 --> 01:02:48.902
<i>So-do</i>

01:03:02.360 --> 01:03:05.454
The mountains are magnificent,
really magnificent.

01:03:05.697 --> 01:03:08.359
- I had them put up just for you.
- Oh?

01:03:08.633 --> 01:03:10.794
Even if it's to a height
of 10,000 feet...

01:03:11.069 --> 01:03:14.596
...Georg always believes in
"rising to the occasion."

01:03:14.873 --> 01:03:17.137
Improve the jokes
or I'll disinvite you.

01:03:17.742 --> 01:03:20.302
You didn't invite me.
I invited myself.

01:03:20.578 --> 01:03:23.103
- Naturally.
- You needed a chaperone...

01:03:23.381 --> 01:03:26.111
...and I needed a place
where the cuisine is superb...

01:03:26.384 --> 01:03:28.978
...the wine cellar unexcelled...

01:03:29.287 --> 01:03:31.881
...and the price perfect.

01:03:32.257 --> 01:03:34.088
Max, you are outrageous.

01:03:34.325 --> 01:03:38.318
Not at all.
I'm a very charming sponge.

01:03:40.965 --> 01:03:42.091
Listen.

01:03:44.436 --> 01:03:46.666
That's the Klopmann Monastery Choir.

01:03:49.674 --> 01:03:51.301
They're good.

01:03:52.343 --> 01:03:53.970
Very good.

01:03:54.779 --> 01:03:57.441
I must explore this area
in the next few days.

01:03:57.649 --> 01:04:01.107
Somewhere, a hungry singing group
is waiting for Max Detweiler...

01:04:01.352 --> 01:04:05.652
...to pluck it out and make it famous
at the Salzburg Folk Festival.

01:04:05.857 --> 01:04:09.156
- They get fame, you get money.
- It's unfair, I admit it.

01:04:09.427 --> 01:04:13.796
But someday that'll be changed.
I shall get the fame too.

01:04:20.839 --> 01:04:23.000
Good heavens, what's this?

01:04:24.442 --> 01:04:26.774
It's nothing.
Just some local urchins.

01:04:41.993 --> 01:04:45.895
This really is exciting for me, Georg.
Being here with you.

01:04:46.731 --> 01:04:49.291
Trees, lakes,
you've seen them before.

01:04:49.567 --> 01:04:52.161
That is not what I mean,
and you know it.

01:04:52.403 --> 01:04:56.362
- You mean me? I'm exciting?
- Is that so impossible?

01:04:56.641 --> 01:04:59.667
No, just highly improbable.

01:04:59.911 --> 01:05:04.075
- There you go, running yourself down.
- Well, I'm a dangerous driver.

01:05:07.852 --> 01:05:11.549
You're much less of a riddle
when I see you here, Georg.

01:05:11.756 --> 01:05:14.589
- In my natural habitat?
- Yes, exactly.

01:05:14.893 --> 01:05:17.020
Are you saying that I'm more
at home...

01:05:17.262 --> 01:05:21.255
...among the birds and the flowers
and the wind that moves...

01:05:21.533 --> 01:05:23.694
...through the trees
like a restless sea?

01:05:23.935 --> 01:05:25.527
How poetic.

01:05:25.737 --> 01:05:27.602
Yes, it was rather, wasn't it?

01:05:28.740 --> 01:05:33.871
More at home here than in Vienna
in all your glittering salons...

01:05:34.078 --> 01:05:38.447
...gossiping gaily with bores I
detest, soaking myself in champagne...

01:05:38.750 --> 01:05:42.447
...stumbling about to waltzes
by Strausses I can't even remember?

01:05:42.754 --> 01:05:44.881
- Is that what you're saying?
- Yes.

01:05:45.123 --> 01:05:47.421
Now whatever gave you that idea?

01:05:50.795 --> 01:05:54.697
Oh, I do like it here, Georg.
It's so lovely and peaceful.

01:05:55.033 --> 01:05:56.967
How can you leave it so often?

01:05:57.235 --> 01:06:00.068
Oh, pretending to be madly active,
I suppose.

01:06:00.305 --> 01:06:03.570
Activity suggests a life
filled with purpose.

01:06:04.309 --> 01:06:06.573
Could it be running away
from memories?

01:06:09.781 --> 01:06:13.717
Or perhaps just searching
for a reason to stay.

01:06:14.385 --> 01:06:17.877
I hope that's why you've been
coming to Vienna so often.

01:06:18.556 --> 01:06:22.890
- Were there other distractions?
- I'd hardly call you a distraction.

01:06:23.127 --> 01:06:25.789
Well, what would you call me, Georg?

01:06:28.066 --> 01:06:29.328
Lovely...

01:06:30.335 --> 01:06:32.963
...charming, witty, graceful,
the perfect hostess...

01:06:33.171 --> 01:06:36.004
...and, you're going to hate me
for this...

01:06:36.441 --> 01:06:38.500
...in a way, my savior.

01:06:38.776 --> 01:06:40.607
Oh, how unromantic.

01:06:40.812 --> 01:06:43.144
I'd be an ungrateful wretch
if I didn't say...

01:06:43.414 --> 01:06:46.645
...that you brought some meaning back
into my life.

01:06:48.486 --> 01:06:51.250
I am amusing, I suppose.

01:06:51.489 --> 01:06:56.256
I have the finest couturier in Vienna
and a glittering circle of friends.

01:06:56.461 --> 01:06:59.589
- I do give some rather gay parties.
- Oh, yes.

01:06:59.831 --> 01:07:01.662
But take all that away...

01:07:01.866 --> 01:07:06.303
...and you have just wealthy,
unattached little me...

01:07:06.971 --> 01:07:09.371
...searching, just like you.

01:07:14.479 --> 01:07:16.174
More strudel, Herr Detweiler?

01:07:16.447 --> 01:07:17.971
- How many have I had?
- Two.

01:07:18.216 --> 01:07:20.150
Make it an uneven three.

01:07:23.454 --> 01:07:26.480
Still eating, Max?
Must be unhappy.

01:07:26.691 --> 01:07:30.650
That mixed quartet I've been trying
to steal away from Sol Hurok...

01:07:30.895 --> 01:07:33.557
- What happened?
...Sascha Petrie stole them first.

01:07:33.798 --> 01:07:35.060
I hate thieves.

01:07:35.333 --> 01:07:38.632
Max, you really must try
and learn to love yourself.

01:07:38.870 --> 01:07:41.202
I had to call Paris, Rome
and Stockholm.

01:07:41.472 --> 01:07:45.033
- On Georg's telephone, of course.
- How else could I afford it?

01:07:45.510 --> 01:07:50.641
I like rich people, the way they live
and how I live when I'm with them.

01:07:50.982 --> 01:07:52.973
I wonder where the children are.

01:07:53.384 --> 01:07:55.875
They must have heard
I was coming and hid.

01:07:56.154 --> 01:07:58.645
I was hoping they'd be here
to welcome you.

01:07:58.890 --> 01:08:03.384
Max, do step out of character for
a moment and try and be charming.

01:08:12.437 --> 01:08:13.836
Well?

01:08:14.739 --> 01:08:15.933
Well what?

01:08:16.174 --> 01:08:19.075
Have you made up his mind?
Do I hear wedding bells?

01:08:19.344 --> 01:08:21.335
- Pealing madly.
- Marvelous.

01:08:21.579 --> 01:08:24.343
- Not necessarily for me.
- What kind of talk's that?

01:08:24.549 --> 01:08:26.107
None-of-your-business talk.

01:08:26.417 --> 01:08:28.851
I'm terribly fond of him,
so don't toy with us.

01:08:29.120 --> 01:08:32.715
But I'm a child. I like toys.
So tell me everything.

01:08:33.024 --> 01:08:38.087
Come on. Tell me every teensy-weensy,
intimate, disgusting detail.

01:08:39.564 --> 01:08:43.694
Well, let's just say I have a feeling
I may be here on approval.

01:08:43.935 --> 01:08:46.961
- I approve of that. How can you miss?
- Far too easily.

01:08:47.238 --> 01:08:50.469
If I know you, darling,
and I do, you will find a way.

01:08:50.742 --> 01:08:53.233
- He's no ordinary man.
- No, he's rich.

01:08:53.478 --> 01:08:55.742
His wife's death gave him
a great heartache.

01:08:55.947 --> 01:08:59.075
And your husband's death
gave you a great fortune.

01:08:59.283 --> 01:09:01.251
Oh, Max, you really are a beast.

01:09:01.452 --> 01:09:05.479
You and Georg are like family.
That's why I want to see you married.

01:09:05.723 --> 01:09:09.284
We must keep all that lovely money
in the family.

01:09:25.576 --> 01:09:28.511
- What are you doing there?
- Oh, Captain von Trapp.

01:09:28.780 --> 01:09:30.805
I was just looking for...

01:09:31.682 --> 01:09:34.515
I didn't see, I mean,
I didn't know you were...

01:09:35.119 --> 01:09:36.814
Heil Hitler!

01:09:37.522 --> 01:09:39.012
Who are you?

01:09:39.290 --> 01:09:41.520
I have a telegram for Herr Detweiler.

01:09:41.793 --> 01:09:44.523
- I am Herr Detweiler.
- Yes, sir.

01:09:49.600 --> 01:09:52.194
You've delivered your telegram.
Now get out.

01:09:58.976 --> 01:10:02.377
- Georg, he's just a boy.
- Yes, and I'm just an Austrian.

01:10:02.613 --> 01:10:05.377
Things will happen.
Make sure they don't happen to you.

01:10:05.683 --> 01:10:08.345
Max! Don't you ever say that again.

01:10:08.619 --> 01:10:10.814
I have no political convictions.

01:10:11.055 --> 01:10:13.990
- Can I help it if other people do?
- You can help it.

01:10:15.126 --> 01:10:17.287
You must help it.

01:10:27.572 --> 01:10:29.164
Hello?

01:10:31.809 --> 01:10:34.573
You're far away. Where are you?

01:10:34.879 --> 01:10:38.747
In a world that's disappearing,
I'm afraid.

01:10:39.584 --> 01:10:43.179
Is there any way I could bring you
back to the world I'm in?

01:11:09.113 --> 01:11:11.604
- Father! Father!
- There's your father!

01:11:12.416 --> 01:11:15.044
Oh, captain, you're home!

01:11:23.427 --> 01:11:26.089
Come out of that water at once!

01:11:35.206 --> 01:11:37.401
Oh, you must be Baroness Schraeder.

01:11:42.713 --> 01:11:45.705
I'm soaked to the skin!

01:11:57.662 --> 01:11:59.061
Straight line!

01:12:13.744 --> 01:12:16.144
This is Baroness Schraeder.

01:12:18.749 --> 01:12:20.512
And these...

01:12:20.751 --> 01:12:22.343
...are my children.

01:12:23.454 --> 01:12:24.944
How do you do?

01:12:26.023 --> 01:12:30.756
Go inside, dry off, clean up, change
your clothes and report back here!

01:12:35.766 --> 01:12:37.859
Fräulein, you will stay here, please!

01:12:39.604 --> 01:12:43.165
I think I'd better go see
what Max is up to.

01:12:53.384 --> 01:12:55.147
Now, fräulein...

01:12:57.054 --> 01:12:59.113
...I want a truthful answer.

01:12:59.523 --> 01:13:00.990
Yes, captain.

01:13:01.292 --> 01:13:05.353
Is it possible,
or could I have just imagined it?

01:13:06.864 --> 01:13:11.358
Have my children, by any chance,
been climbing trees today?

01:13:11.836 --> 01:13:12.996
Yes, captain.

01:13:14.071 --> 01:13:15.402
I see.

01:13:15.973 --> 01:13:20.467
And where, may I ask,
did they get these...

01:13:20.745 --> 01:13:22.804
- Play clothes.
- Is that what they are?

01:13:23.014 --> 01:13:26.415
I made them from the drapes
that used to hang in my bedroom.

01:13:27.218 --> 01:13:29.345
- Drapes?
- They have plenty of wear left.

01:13:29.553 --> 01:13:31.487
We've been everywhere in them.

01:13:31.722 --> 01:13:36.182
Are you telling me that my children
have been roaming about Salzburg...

01:13:36.394 --> 01:13:39.761
...dressed up in nothing
but some old drapes?

01:13:39.997 --> 01:13:41.658
And having a marvelous time!

01:13:41.866 --> 01:13:45.097
- They have uniforms.
- Forgive me, straitjackets.

01:13:45.336 --> 01:13:48.100
They can't be children
if they worry about clothes...

01:13:48.372 --> 01:13:49.498
They don't complain.

01:13:49.740 --> 01:13:52.436
They don't dare.
They love you too much and fear...

01:13:52.677 --> 01:13:54.235
Don't discuss my children.

01:13:54.445 --> 01:13:56.379
You've got to hear, you're
never home...

01:13:56.580 --> 01:13:58.104
I don't want to hear more!

01:13:58.349 --> 01:14:00.840
I know you don't, but you've got to!

01:14:01.619 --> 01:14:03.780
- Liesl's not a child.
- Not one word...

01:14:04.055 --> 01:14:06.922
Soon she'll be a woman
and you won't even know her.

01:14:07.191 --> 01:14:10.251
Friedrich wants to be a man
but you're not here to show...

01:14:10.528 --> 01:14:11.859
Don't you dare tell me...

01:14:12.096 --> 01:14:15.361
Brigitta could tell you about him.
She notices everything.

01:14:15.599 --> 01:14:18.727
Kurt acts tough to hide the pain
when you ignore him...

01:14:18.936 --> 01:14:20.460
...the way you do all of them.

01:14:20.738 --> 01:14:23.138
Louisa, I don't know about yet.

01:14:23.407 --> 01:14:26.604
The little ones just want love.
Please, love them all.

01:14:26.877 --> 01:14:28.401
I don't care to hear more.

01:14:28.646 --> 01:14:32.742
- I am not finished yet, captain!
- Oh, yes, you are, captain!

01:14:34.285 --> 01:14:35.445
Fräulein.

01:14:36.754 --> 01:14:40.884
Now, you will pack
your things this minute...

01:14:41.092 --> 01:14:43.583
...and return to the abbey.

01:14:46.230 --> 01:14:47.561
What's that?

01:14:49.300 --> 01:14:50.324
It's singing.

01:14:50.968 --> 01:14:53.766
Yes, I realize it's singing.
But who is singing?

01:14:54.739 --> 01:14:56.297
The children.

01:14:59.176 --> 01:15:00.507
The children?

01:15:01.078 --> 01:15:03.808
I taught them something to sing
for the baroness.

01:15:09.453 --> 01:15:15.483
<i>My heart wants to sing</i>
<i>Every song it hears</i>

01:15:15.760 --> 01:15:18.320
<i>Every song that it hears</i>

01:15:18.596 --> 01:15:24.034
<i>My heart wants to beat like the wings</i>
<i>Of the birds that rise</i>

01:15:24.301 --> 01:15:27.429
<i>From the lake to the trees</i>

01:15:27.671 --> 01:15:29.104
<i>To the trees</i>

01:15:29.340 --> 01:15:34.277
<i>My heart wants to sigh</i>
<i>Like a chime that flies</i>

01:15:34.478 --> 01:15:39.108
<i>From a church on a breeze</i>

01:15:39.383 --> 01:15:43.285
<i>To laugh like a brook</i>
<i>When it trips and falls</i>

01:15:43.554 --> 01:15:46.489
<i>Over stones on its way</i>

01:15:46.791 --> 01:15:48.156
<i>On its way</i>

01:15:48.392 --> 01:15:52.829
<i>To sing through the night</i>

01:15:53.030 --> 01:15:58.696
<i>Like a lark who is learning to pray</i>

01:15:58.969 --> 01:16:03.463
<i>I go to the hills</i>

01:16:03.674 --> 01:16:09.909
<i>When my heart is lonely</i>

01:16:10.181 --> 01:16:13.878
<i>I know I will hear</i>

01:16:14.151 --> 01:16:19.919
<i>What I've heard before</i>

01:16:20.758 --> 01:16:24.990
<i>My heart will be blessed</i>

01:16:25.229 --> 01:16:32.192
<i>With the sound of music</i>

01:16:33.070 --> 01:16:38.269
<i>And I'll sing...</i>

01:16:38.509 --> 01:16:46.609
<i>...once more</i>

01:17:19.884 --> 01:17:21.647
Edelweiss!

01:17:25.623 --> 01:17:28.786
You never told me how enchanting
your children are.

01:17:37.401 --> 01:17:38.959
Don't go away.

01:17:44.074 --> 01:17:45.473
Fräulein.

01:17:48.812 --> 01:17:50.006
I...

01:17:51.482 --> 01:17:54.280
...behaved badly. I apologize.

01:17:56.020 --> 01:17:59.615
I'm far too outspoken.
It's one of my worst faults.

01:18:00.024 --> 01:18:01.491
You were right.

01:18:03.961 --> 01:18:05.861
I don't know my children.

01:18:07.164 --> 01:18:11.294
There's still time, captain.
They want so much to be close to you.

01:18:11.635 --> 01:18:15.503
And you brought music back
into the house.

01:18:16.840 --> 01:18:18.273
I'd forgotten.

01:18:21.011 --> 01:18:22.342
Fräulein.

01:18:24.848 --> 01:18:26.110
I want you to stay.

01:18:30.120 --> 01:18:32.850
I ask you to stay.

01:18:34.692 --> 01:18:38.184
- If I could be of any help.
- You have already.

01:18:38.796 --> 01:18:39.854
More than you know.

01:18:59.583 --> 01:19:00.914
Marta.

01:19:01.652 --> 01:19:02.880
Curtain!

01:19:05.556 --> 01:19:08.889
<i>High on a hill was a lonely goatherd</i>

01:19:10.394 --> 01:19:13.659
<i>Loud was the voice</i>
<i>Of the lonely goatherd</i>

01:19:15.165 --> 01:19:18.430
<i>Folks in a town</i>
<i>That was quite remote heard</i>

01:19:20.004 --> 01:19:23.235
<i>Lusty and clear</i>
<i>From the goatherd's throat heard</i>

01:19:34.752 --> 01:19:37.619
Marta. Marta!

01:19:40.024 --> 01:19:42.015
Gretl, the prince!

01:19:43.761 --> 01:19:47.219
<i>A prince on the bridge</i>
<i>Of a castle moat heard</i>

01:19:48.699 --> 01:19:51.031
<i>Men on a road</i>
<i>With a load to tote heard</i>

01:19:53.537 --> 01:19:56.802
<i>Men in the midst</i>
<i>Of a table d'hôte heard</i>

01:19:58.142 --> 01:20:01.407
<i>Men drinking beer</i>
<i>With the foam afloat heard</i>

01:20:12.489 --> 01:20:15.617
<i>One little girl</i>
<i>In a pale pink coat heard</i>

01:20:17.261 --> 01:20:20.594
<i>She yodeled back</i>
<i>To the lonely goatherd</i>

01:20:21.765 --> 01:20:25.166
<i>Soon her mama</i>
<i>With a gleaming gloat heard</i>

01:20:26.670 --> 01:20:29.969
<i>What a duet for a girl and goatherd</i>

01:21:16.553 --> 01:21:19.818
<i>One little girl</i>
<i>In a pale pink coat heard</i>

01:21:21.358 --> 01:21:24.623
<i>She yodeled back</i>
<i>To the lonely goatherd</i>

01:21:25.963 --> 01:21:29.399
<i>Soon her mama</i>
<i>With a gleaming gloat heard</i>

01:21:30.868 --> 01:21:33.996
<i>What a duet for a girl and goatherd</i>

01:21:35.706 --> 01:21:37.333
<i>Happy are they</i>

01:21:40.310 --> 01:21:43.575
<i>Soon the duet will become a trio</i>

01:22:08.071 --> 01:22:09.663
- Bravo!
- Bravo!

01:22:09.873 --> 01:22:11.363
Very good!

01:22:13.177 --> 01:22:15.077
Wonderful!

01:22:15.679 --> 01:22:18.842
- Can we keep the puppets, Uncle Max?
- Yes, can we?

01:22:19.049 --> 01:22:21.074
Of course you may, my darlings.

01:22:21.285 --> 01:22:25.517
Why else did I tell Professor Kohner
to send the bill to your father?

01:22:29.259 --> 01:22:30.920
Well done, fräulein.

01:22:33.430 --> 01:22:35.398
I really am very much impressed.

01:22:35.599 --> 01:22:37.590
They're your children, captain.

01:22:44.808 --> 01:22:47.106
My dear, is there anything
you can't do?

01:22:47.377 --> 01:22:49.709
Well, I'm not sure
I'll make a good nun.

01:22:49.947 --> 01:22:53.041
If you have any problems,
I'd be happy to help you.

01:22:56.153 --> 01:22:57.586
Attention, everyone!

01:22:57.788 --> 01:23:01.246
I have an announcement to make.
Surprise! Surprise!

01:23:01.491 --> 01:23:03.789
Today, after a long
and desperate search...

01:23:04.061 --> 01:23:09.055
...I have found a most exciting
entry for the Salzburg Folk Festival.

01:23:09.266 --> 01:23:11.097
Congratulations, Max.

01:23:11.335 --> 01:23:14.304
And who will you
be exploiting this time?

01:23:16.106 --> 01:23:19.303
- The Saint Ignatius Choir?
- Guess again.

01:23:20.010 --> 01:23:23.946
Well, let me see now.
The Klopmann Choir?

01:23:24.181 --> 01:23:26.581
- No, no, no, no.
- No, no?

01:23:26.783 --> 01:23:27.977
Tell us.

01:23:28.185 --> 01:23:31.643
A singing group all in one family.
You'll never guess, Georg.

01:23:31.922 --> 01:23:34.823
What a charming idea!

01:23:35.025 --> 01:23:36.822
Whose family?

01:23:37.694 --> 01:23:39.321
Yours.

01:23:39.529 --> 01:23:41.861
They'll be the talk of the festival.

01:23:44.701 --> 01:23:47.693
- Well, now, what's so funny?
- You are, Max.

01:23:47.971 --> 01:23:51.099
You're expensive, but very funny.

01:23:51.842 --> 01:23:54.174
- They'll be a sensation!
- No, Max.

01:23:54.444 --> 01:23:56.639
It's a wonderful idea.
Fresh, original.

01:23:56.847 --> 01:24:01.648
Max! My children
do not sing in public.

01:24:02.319 --> 01:24:04.287
You can't blame me for trying.

01:24:04.488 --> 01:24:07.480
Children, who shall we hear
from next?

01:24:10.294 --> 01:24:11.454
Who?

01:24:17.634 --> 01:24:18.828
Yes.

01:24:21.705 --> 01:24:23.639
The vote is unanimous.

01:24:24.474 --> 01:24:26.032
You, captain.

01:24:26.310 --> 01:24:27.504
Me?

01:24:28.345 --> 01:24:30.643
- I don't understand.
- Please.

01:24:36.853 --> 01:24:38.980
No, no, no, no.

01:24:39.256 --> 01:24:41.315
I'm told that you were quite good.

01:24:41.525 --> 01:24:44.824
- That was a very, very long time ago.
- I remember, Father.

01:24:45.062 --> 01:24:47.929
- Play us something we know.
- Oh, please, Father.

01:24:50.867 --> 01:24:51.925
Well...

01:25:02.179 --> 01:25:04.340
- Why didn't you tell me?
- What?

01:25:04.614 --> 01:25:06.912
To bring along my harmonica.

01:25:09.252 --> 01:25:11.379
<i>Edelweiss</i>

01:25:12.956 --> 01:25:15.254
<i>Edelweiss</i>

01:25:16.360 --> 01:25:22.560
<i>Every morning you greet me</i>

01:25:22.799 --> 01:25:25.859
<i>Small and white</i>

01:25:26.703 --> 01:25:30.070
<i>Clean and bright</i>

01:25:30.273 --> 01:25:33.106
<i>You look happy...</i>

01:25:33.310 --> 01:25:37.144
<i>...to meet me</i>

01:25:37.414 --> 01:25:39.712
<i>Blossom of snow</i>

01:25:39.983 --> 01:25:44.113
<i>May you bloom and grow</i>

01:25:44.321 --> 01:25:50.658
<i>Bloom and grow forever</i>

01:25:51.628 --> 01:25:55.325
<i>Edelweiss</i>

01:25:55.565 --> 01:25:58.159
<i>Edelweiss</i>

01:25:58.835 --> 01:26:06.105
<i>Bless my homeland forever</i>

01:26:10.480 --> 01:26:13.677
<i>- Edelweiss</i>
<i>- Edelweiss</i>

01:26:13.984 --> 01:26:17.476
<i>- Edelweiss</i>
<i>- Edelweiss</i>

01:26:17.687 --> 01:26:24.092
<i>Every morning you greet me</i>

01:26:24.327 --> 01:26:27.854
<i>- Small and white</i>
<i>- Small and white</i>

01:26:28.131 --> 01:26:31.589
<i>- Clean and bright</i>
<i>- Clean and bright</i>

01:26:31.802 --> 01:26:34.293
<i>You look happy...</i>

01:26:34.538 --> 01:26:38.167
<i>...to meet me</i>

01:26:38.642 --> 01:26:40.769
<i>Blossom of snow</i>

01:26:40.977 --> 01:26:45.141
<i>May you bloom and grow</i>

01:26:45.382 --> 01:26:52.447
<i>Bloom and grow forever</i>

01:26:52.689 --> 01:26:56.318
<i>Edelweiss</i>

01:26:56.560 --> 01:26:59.222
<i>Edelweiss</i>

01:26:59.830 --> 01:27:09.728
<i>Bless my homeland forever</i>

01:27:19.015 --> 01:27:22.678
Anytime you say the word, Georg,
you can be part of my new act:

01:27:22.886 --> 01:27:25.377
The von Trapp Family Singers.

01:27:26.490 --> 01:27:28.981
I have a wonderful idea, Georg.

01:27:29.226 --> 01:27:31.694
Let's really fill this house
with music.

01:27:31.928 --> 01:27:34.897
You must give a grand
and glorious party for me.

01:27:35.165 --> 01:27:37.861
- A party?
- Yes, Father, please!

01:27:38.068 --> 01:27:40.434
It's high time
I met all your friends...

01:27:40.737 --> 01:27:43.228
...and they met me.
Don't you agree?

01:27:43.507 --> 01:27:45.737
- I see what you mean.
- Oh, please!

01:27:46.009 --> 01:27:49.172
Children, it's bedtime.
Come now, say good night.

01:27:50.113 --> 01:27:51.410
Good night, Father.

01:27:51.615 --> 01:27:54.448
- Good night.
- Good night, Baroness Schraeder.

01:27:54.684 --> 01:27:56.242
Good night, Father.

01:27:59.222 --> 01:28:01.053
Good night, Uncle Max.

01:28:02.959 --> 01:28:06.122
It'll be my first party, Father!

01:28:38.662 --> 01:28:41.290
- Captain.
- Herr Zeller. Baroness Schraeder.

01:28:41.498 --> 01:28:44.626
- Good evening, Herr Zeller.
- Baroness.

01:28:45.936 --> 01:28:48.404
How do you do? Good evening.

01:29:09.025 --> 01:29:12.461
Did you notice the obvious
display of the Austrian flag?

01:29:19.536 --> 01:29:21.333
The women look so beautiful.

01:29:21.605 --> 01:29:22.936
I think they look ugly.

01:29:23.206 --> 01:29:25.037
You're just scared of them.

01:29:25.275 --> 01:29:27.505
Silly, only grown-up men fear women.

01:29:28.111 --> 01:29:31.672
- I think the men look beautiful.
- How would you know?

01:29:48.965 --> 01:29:50.990
Liesl, who are you dancing with?

01:29:51.201 --> 01:29:52.828
Nobody.

01:29:53.637 --> 01:29:55.537
Oh, yes, you are.

01:29:58.008 --> 01:29:59.498
May I have this dance?

01:29:59.709 --> 01:30:02.200
I'd be delighted, young man.

01:30:08.985 --> 01:30:11.647
Why didn't you tell me
you could dance?

01:30:11.888 --> 01:30:16.825
We feared you'd make us all dance.
The von Trapp Family Dancers.

01:30:21.231 --> 01:30:22.926
What are they playing?

01:30:23.166 --> 01:30:25.794
It's the Laendler.
An Austrian folk dance.

01:30:26.002 --> 01:30:29.165
- Show me.
- I haven't danced since I was little.

01:30:29.372 --> 01:30:31.340
You remember. Please?

01:30:31.608 --> 01:30:33.542
- Well...
- Please.

01:30:33.777 --> 01:30:36.007
All right. Come on over here.

01:30:36.513 --> 01:30:39.346
Now you bow and I curtsy.

01:30:40.283 --> 01:30:43.218
- Like this?
- Fine. Now we go for a little walk.

01:30:43.453 --> 01:30:46.115
One, two, three. One, two, three.

01:30:46.423 --> 01:30:51.019
One, two, three, step together.
Now, step hop, step hop.

01:30:51.261 --> 01:30:53.923
Now turn under. Not quite.

01:30:54.130 --> 01:30:58.089
This way. Hop step, hop.
And under.

01:30:58.768 --> 01:31:00.463
Kurt, we'll have to practice.

01:31:00.704 --> 01:31:02.194
Do allow me, will you?

01:32:30.493 --> 01:32:32.358
I don't remember anymore.

01:32:34.531 --> 01:32:36.726
- Your face is all red.
- Is it?

01:32:38.067 --> 01:32:40.160
I don't suppose I'm used to dancing.

01:32:42.872 --> 01:32:44.863
Why, that was beautifully done.

01:32:45.141 --> 01:32:47.041
What a lovely couple you make.

01:32:47.243 --> 01:32:49.370
It's time the children
said good night.

01:32:49.646 --> 01:32:50.977
We'll be in the hall.

01:32:51.214 --> 01:32:54.081
- We have something special prepared.
- Right!

01:32:54.384 --> 01:32:55.544
Yes, come on!

01:33:02.392 --> 01:33:04.724
All that needless worrying, Georg.

01:33:04.994 --> 01:33:08.020
You thought you wouldn't find
a friend at the party.

01:33:10.934 --> 01:33:14.529
- A bit chilly out tonight, isn't it?
- Oh, I don't know.

01:33:14.737 --> 01:33:16.762
It seemed rather warm to me.

01:33:20.944 --> 01:33:22.172
Ladies and gentlemen.

01:33:22.912 --> 01:33:27.008
The children of Captain von Trapp
wish to say good night to you.

01:33:41.130 --> 01:33:45.032
<i>There's a sad sort of clanging</i>
<i>From the clock in the hall</i>

01:33:45.235 --> 01:33:48.966
<i>And the bells in the steeple too</i>

01:33:49.239 --> 01:33:53.266
<i>And up in the nursery</i>
<i>An absurd little bird</i>

01:33:53.476 --> 01:33:55.910
<i>Is popping up to say "coo-coo"</i>

01:33:56.145 --> 01:33:57.806
<i>Coo-coo</i>

01:33:58.081 --> 01:33:59.309
<i>Coo-coo</i>

01:33:59.549 --> 01:34:01.710
<i>Regretfully they tell us</i>

01:34:01.918 --> 01:34:03.283
<i>But firmly they compel us</i>

01:34:03.553 --> 01:34:06.613
<i>To say goodbye</i>

01:34:06.823 --> 01:34:12.125
<i>To you</i>

01:34:15.331 --> 01:34:19.233
<i>So long, farewell</i>
<i>Auf Wiedersehen, good night</i>

01:34:19.435 --> 01:34:23.303
<i>I hate to go</i>
<i>And leave this pretty sight</i>

01:34:30.580 --> 01:34:33.913
<i>So long, farewell,</i>
<i>Auf Wiedersehen, adieu</i>

01:34:34.584 --> 01:34:38.111
<i>Adieu, adieu</i>
<i>To you and you and you</i>

01:34:45.461 --> 01:34:49.261
<i>So long, farewell</i>
<i>Au revoir, auf Wiedersehen</i>

01:34:49.532 --> 01:34:53.468
<i>I'd like to stay</i>
<i>And taste my first champagne</i>

01:34:53.703 --> 01:34:56.137
- Yes?
- No.

01:35:00.476 --> 01:35:04.139
<i>So long, farewell</i>
<i>Auf Wiedersehen, goodbye</i>

01:35:04.480 --> 01:35:08.439
<i>I leave and heave a sigh</i>
<i>And say goodbye</i>

01:35:08.651 --> 01:35:12.644
<i>Goodbye</i>

01:35:15.692 --> 01:35:18.786
<i>I'm glad to go</i>

01:35:19.028 --> 01:35:21.895
<i>I cannot tell a lie</i>

01:35:22.231 --> 01:35:25.223
<i>I flit, I float</i>

01:35:25.501 --> 01:35:28.959
<i>I fleetly flee, I fly</i>

01:35:39.015 --> 01:35:44.749
<i>The sun has gone to bed</i>

01:35:44.988 --> 01:35:48.719
<i>And so must I</i>

01:35:48.925 --> 01:35:51.325
<i>So long</i>

01:35:51.561 --> 01:35:54.121
<i>Farewell</i>

01:35:54.330 --> 01:35:59.734
<i>Auf Wiedersehen, goodbye</i>

01:36:00.003 --> 01:36:05.339
<i>Goodbye</i>

01:36:06.042 --> 01:36:11.605
<i>Goodbye</i>

01:36:11.848 --> 01:36:18.720
<i>Goodbye</i>

01:36:18.921 --> 01:36:27.420
<i>Goodbye</i>

01:36:32.435 --> 01:36:35.199
Extraordinary!
What they'd do at the festival.

01:36:35.438 --> 01:36:37.929
Young lady,
I must have a word with you.

01:36:38.941 --> 01:36:42.934
Georg, you won't let this girl
get away. She must join the party.

01:36:43.212 --> 01:36:45.612
- No, really l...
- Stop. Stop it now.

01:36:45.882 --> 01:36:48.817
- Georg, please.
- You can if you want to, fräulein.

01:36:49.052 --> 01:36:51.543
I insist.
You will be my dinner partner.

01:36:51.754 --> 01:36:53.654
This is business.
Franz...

01:36:53.923 --> 01:36:57.086
...set another place next to mine
for Fräulein Maria.

01:36:59.262 --> 01:37:01.992
- Whatever you say.
- It appears to be all arranged.

01:37:02.799 --> 01:37:04.664
- It does.
- I'm not suitably dressed.

01:37:05.735 --> 01:37:07.225
You can change. We'll wait.

01:37:10.840 --> 01:37:13.775
Captain, you must be very proud
of your youngsters.

01:37:13.976 --> 01:37:14.840
I am, thank you.

01:37:15.111 --> 01:37:19.673
Is there a more beautiful expression
of what is good in our country...

01:37:19.916 --> 01:37:23.352
...than the innocent voices
of our children?

01:37:23.753 --> 01:37:25.118
Oh, come now, baron.

01:37:25.354 --> 01:37:29.120
Would you have us believe that Austria
holds a monopoly on virtue?

01:37:30.026 --> 01:37:34.156
Herr Zeller, some of us prefer
Austrian voices raised in song...

01:37:34.363 --> 01:37:36.763
...to ugly German threats.

01:37:37.834 --> 01:37:41.463
The ostrich buries his head
in the sand...

01:37:41.671 --> 01:37:44.606
...and sometimes in the flag.

01:37:45.141 --> 01:37:49.339
Perhaps those who would warn you that
the Anschluss is coming, and it is...

01:37:49.612 --> 01:37:53.309
...would get further with you by setting
their words to music.

01:37:53.516 --> 01:37:58.180
If the Nazis take over Austria, you
will be the entire trumpet section.

01:37:58.488 --> 01:37:59.512
You flatter me.

01:38:00.556 --> 01:38:04.458
Oh, how clumsy of me.
I meant to accuse you.

01:38:12.201 --> 01:38:14.692
It's very kind of you
to offer to help me, baroness.

01:38:14.971 --> 01:38:16.529
I'm delighted, Maria.

01:38:17.006 --> 01:38:20.703
I really don't think I have anything
that would be appropriate.

01:38:21.177 --> 01:38:25.307
Now where is that lovely little thing
you were wearing the other evening?

01:38:25.548 --> 01:38:28.847
When the captain couldn't keep
his eyes off you.

01:38:32.221 --> 01:38:34.052
Couldn't keep his eyes off me?

01:38:35.391 --> 01:38:37.188
Come, my dear, we are women.

01:38:37.426 --> 01:38:40.827
Let's not pretend we don't know
when a man notices us.

01:38:41.063 --> 01:38:44.499
- Here we are.
- The captain notices everybody.

01:38:45.067 --> 01:38:47.501
There's no need to feel
so defensive, Maria.

01:38:47.737 --> 01:38:50.205
You are quite attractive, you know.

01:38:50.439 --> 01:38:54.068
The captain would hardly be a man
if he didn't notice you.

01:38:55.678 --> 01:38:58.044
Baroness, I hope you're joking.

01:38:58.514 --> 01:38:59.776
Not at all.

01:39:00.016 --> 01:39:01.608
I've never done a thing to...

01:39:01.884 --> 01:39:03.442
You don't have to, my dear.

01:39:04.086 --> 01:39:08.921
Nothing's more irresistible to a man
than a woman who's in love with him.

01:39:10.193 --> 01:39:12.627
- In love with him?
- Of course.

01:39:13.563 --> 01:39:16.964
What makes it so nice is
he thinks he's in love with you.

01:39:19.702 --> 01:39:21.294
But that's not true.

01:39:21.704 --> 01:39:25.196
Surely you've noticed the way
he looks into your eyes.

01:39:25.474 --> 01:39:30.377
And you know, you blushed in his arms
when you were dancing just now.

01:39:31.614 --> 01:39:33.309
Don't take it to heart.

01:39:33.583 --> 01:39:35.881
He'll get over it soon enough,
I think.

01:39:36.152 --> 01:39:38.120
Men do, you know.

01:39:39.121 --> 01:39:40.213
Then I should go.

01:39:41.557 --> 01:39:42.990
I mustn't stay here.

01:39:53.469 --> 01:39:56.905
- Is there something I can do to help?
- No, nothing.

01:39:58.674 --> 01:39:59.902
Yes.

01:40:00.910 --> 01:40:02.935
Don't say a word to the captain.

01:40:04.580 --> 01:40:08.141
No, I wouldn't dream of it.

01:40:14.924 --> 01:40:16.482
Goodbye, Maria.

01:40:17.293 --> 01:40:20.091
I'm sure you'll make a very fine nun.

01:40:50.126 --> 01:40:52.117
Champagne, darling.

01:40:52.528 --> 01:40:56.521
I feel like celebrating. Cheers.

01:41:02.004 --> 01:41:04.905
- You know something.
- Perhaps.

01:41:05.141 --> 01:41:09.669
If you're so clever, tell me how to
get fräulein to influence Georg.

01:41:09.912 --> 01:41:12.540
I want those children in the festival.

01:41:13.015 --> 01:41:15.313
Elsa, this is important to Austria.

01:41:15.518 --> 01:41:17.213
Wouldn't do you any harm either.

01:41:17.420 --> 01:41:19.012
I thought of that.

01:41:19.255 --> 01:41:21.723
Well, if it's a matter of influence...

01:41:21.924 --> 01:41:24.825
...maybe the one you have
to be talking to is me.

01:44:49.758 --> 01:44:51.988
- Two.
- Three.

01:44:52.260 --> 01:44:53.750
- Four.
- Five.

01:44:54.996 --> 01:44:57.021
- Six.
- Seven.

01:44:57.298 --> 01:44:58.925
Eight.

01:44:59.167 --> 01:45:00.998
- Four.
- Two.

01:45:02.103 --> 01:45:03.934
- Seven.
- Five.

01:45:04.172 --> 01:45:06.367
- Two.
- Six.

01:45:11.012 --> 01:45:13.037
Isn't this fun?

01:45:14.449 --> 01:45:16.781
- Four.
- I'm number five.

01:45:17.051 --> 01:45:19.212
- Oh, yes.
- Eight.

01:45:19.521 --> 01:45:21.887
- Two.
- Four.

01:45:22.290 --> 01:45:23.518
Six.

01:45:25.994 --> 01:45:27.222
Two.

01:45:28.363 --> 01:45:31.332
Baroness Schraeder, do you mind
if we stop now? We're tired.

01:45:31.566 --> 01:45:33.534
Whatever you want, dear.

01:45:33.802 --> 01:45:35.793
We'll do it again tomorrow.

01:45:45.980 --> 01:45:48.141
The country's so restful, isn't it?

01:45:49.184 --> 01:45:50.811
Have some lemonade.

01:45:52.053 --> 01:45:53.486
There must be an easier way.

01:45:54.889 --> 01:45:58.154
I get a fiendish delight thinking
of you as the mother of seven.

01:45:59.093 --> 01:46:00.924
How do you plan to do it?

01:46:01.196 --> 01:46:03.221
Darling, haven't you ever heard...

01:46:03.498 --> 01:46:06.592
...of a delightful little thing
called boarding school?

01:46:07.735 --> 01:46:09.999
Baroness Machiavelli.

01:46:11.339 --> 01:46:13.330
Uncle Max, where's Father?

01:46:13.608 --> 01:46:15.405
I think he's in the house.

01:46:15.610 --> 01:46:18.170
What's the matter
with all you gloomy pussies?

01:46:18.413 --> 01:46:21.211
- Nothing.
- I know. Let's have a rehearsal.

01:46:21.416 --> 01:46:22.314
What for?

01:46:22.517 --> 01:46:25.008
Let's make believe we're on-stage
at the festival.

01:46:25.220 --> 01:46:29.088
- I don't feel like singing.
- Not without Fräulein Maria.

01:46:29.357 --> 01:46:31.757
Liesl, get the guitar.
Come on, Marta.

01:46:31.960 --> 01:46:34.929
Everybody into the group.
Get in your places.

01:46:35.196 --> 01:46:37.960
Now be cheerful, right?
Give us the key, Liesl.

01:46:39.868 --> 01:46:42.530
Now, impress me.

01:46:46.541 --> 01:46:47.872
Gretl, why don't you sing?

01:46:48.142 --> 01:46:50.610
I can't. I've got a sore finger.

01:46:51.646 --> 01:46:54.706
But you sang so beautifully
the night of the party.

01:46:54.916 --> 01:46:57.248
Come on, all of you.
Try something you know.

01:46:57.485 --> 01:46:58.975
Enjoy it. Be cheerful.

01:46:59.254 --> 01:47:00.881
All right, Liesl.

01:47:02.824 --> 01:47:08.228
<i>The hills are alive</i>

01:47:08.463 --> 01:47:16.131
<i>With the sound of music</i>

01:47:17.338 --> 01:47:22.401
<i>With songs they have sung</i>

01:47:22.644 --> 01:47:30.483
<i>For a thousand years</i>

01:47:31.185 --> 01:47:36.589
<i>The hills fill my heart</i>

01:47:36.824 --> 01:47:44.526
<i>With the sound of music</i>

01:47:44.866 --> 01:47:47.494
They wanted to sing for me,
bless their hearts.

01:47:47.802 --> 01:47:49.702
That's lovely, lovely.
Don't stop.

01:47:53.708 --> 01:47:57.610
- Something long and cool, Georg?
- No, thank you, darling.

01:47:58.012 --> 01:48:00.446
- Father?
- Yes, Brigitta?

01:48:00.882 --> 01:48:03.146
Is it true Fräulein Maria
isn't coming back?

01:48:03.451 --> 01:48:06.545
Yes, I suppose it's true.
What have we got here?

01:48:06.854 --> 01:48:11.553
- Pink lemonade.
- Laced with lemonade.

01:48:12.293 --> 01:48:13.817
I don't believe it, Father.

01:48:15.196 --> 01:48:17.221
- What?
- About Fräulein Maria.

01:48:17.632 --> 01:48:18.860
Oh, Fräulein Maria!

01:48:19.167 --> 01:48:22.625
Didn't I tell you what her note said?
I'm sure I did.

01:48:23.371 --> 01:48:25.862
She said she missed her life
at the abbey.

01:48:26.140 --> 01:48:28.301
She had to leave us.

01:48:28.543 --> 01:48:30.135
And that's all there is to it.

01:48:31.846 --> 01:48:34.542
I think I'm brave enough to try
some of that.

01:48:34.749 --> 01:48:37.479
- She didn't even say goodbye.
- She did in her note.

01:48:37.752 --> 01:48:39.549
That isn't the same thing.

01:48:39.854 --> 01:48:41.481
Not too sweet, not too sour.

01:48:42.223 --> 01:48:44.214
Just too pink.

01:48:45.660 --> 01:48:48.754
Father, who is our new governess
going to be?

01:48:55.403 --> 01:48:56.495
Well...

01:48:58.840 --> 01:49:04.073
...you're not going to have
a governess anymore.

01:49:04.412 --> 01:49:07.074
- We're not?
- No.

01:49:09.283 --> 01:49:11.410
You're going to have a new mother.

01:49:12.520 --> 01:49:14.545
A new mother?

01:49:15.390 --> 01:49:18.518
We talked about it last night.
It's all settled.

01:49:18.726 --> 01:49:21.422
And we're all going to be very happy.

01:49:54.429 --> 01:49:56.897
Well, all right, all right.
Run off and play.

01:50:28.863 --> 01:50:29.830
Yes, my children?

01:50:30.031 --> 01:50:32.431
- My name is Liesl.
- Yes, Liesl?

01:50:32.934 --> 01:50:36.870
We, my brothers and sisters,
want to see Fräulein Maria.

01:50:38.039 --> 01:50:40.030
Fräulein Maria?

01:50:40.808 --> 01:50:42.776
Oh, Maria.

01:50:44.679 --> 01:50:46.510
Come in, please.

01:50:50.384 --> 01:50:51.942
Wait here.

01:51:02.897 --> 01:51:06.060
I'm Sister Margaretta. I understand
you inquired about Maria.

01:51:06.334 --> 01:51:08.825
We have to see her.
Will you tell her we're here?

01:51:09.070 --> 01:51:11.664
- I'm afraid I can't do that.
- But you've got to!

01:51:11.973 --> 01:51:14.032
- She's our governess.
- We want her back.

01:51:14.242 --> 01:51:16.142
She didn't even say goodbye.

01:51:16.377 --> 01:51:18.140
All we want to do is talk to her.

01:51:18.913 --> 01:51:21.814
I'm very sorry,
but Maria is in seclusion.

01:51:22.049 --> 01:51:25.143
- She hasn't been seeing anyone.
- She'll see us.

01:51:25.386 --> 01:51:27.877
I want to show her my finger.

01:51:28.089 --> 01:51:29.989
Some other time, dear.

01:51:30.258 --> 01:51:31.555
I'll tell her you were here.

01:51:31.826 --> 01:51:34.886
- It was sweet of you to call.
- We have to speak to her!

01:51:35.530 --> 01:51:38.658
Run along, children.
Run along home.

01:51:38.866 --> 01:51:40.493
I'm sure she'd like to see us.

01:51:40.768 --> 01:51:43.032
Sister Margaretta, please.

01:51:43.271 --> 01:51:47.002
- Goodbye, children.
- Sister Margaretta, may we, please?

01:51:49.777 --> 01:51:51.506
What was that about, Sister?

01:51:51.746 --> 01:51:53.941
The von Trapp children,
Reverend Mother.

01:51:54.182 --> 01:51:56.616
They want to see Maria.

01:51:56.884 --> 01:51:59.182
Has she spoken yet?
Has she told you anything?

01:51:59.453 --> 01:52:03.446
She doesn't say a word,
Reverend Mother, except in prayer.

01:52:03.724 --> 01:52:04.713
Poor child.

01:52:04.926 --> 01:52:07.895
It's strange.
She seems happy to be back here...

01:52:08.129 --> 01:52:11.428
...and yet she's unhappy too.

01:52:12.700 --> 01:52:15.760
Perhaps I have been wrong
in leaving her alone so long.

01:52:16.037 --> 01:52:18.733
Bring her to me,
even if she's not yet ready.

01:52:18.940 --> 01:52:20.601
Yes, Reverend Mother.

01:52:26.113 --> 01:52:29.605
Sister Augusta, take our new postulant
to the robing room.

01:52:30.618 --> 01:52:32.882
God bless you, my daughter.

01:52:39.093 --> 01:52:40.822
Yes, bring her in.

01:52:49.837 --> 01:52:52.101
You've been unhappy. I'm sorry.

01:52:54.141 --> 01:52:55.335
Reverend Mother.

01:52:55.676 --> 01:52:58.304
Why did they send you back to us?

01:52:59.146 --> 01:53:01.114
They didn't send me back.
I left.

01:53:03.618 --> 01:53:05.176
Sit down, Maria.

01:53:05.686 --> 01:53:07.483
Tell me what happened.

01:53:12.693 --> 01:53:14.024
I was frightened.

01:53:14.295 --> 01:53:18.755
- Frightened? Were they unkind to you.
- Oh, no!

01:53:19.000 --> 01:53:22.697
No, I was confused. I felt...

01:53:24.171 --> 01:53:26.264
I've never felt that way before.

01:53:26.507 --> 01:53:30.273
I couldn't stay. I knew that here
I'd be away from it. I'd be safe.

01:53:30.511 --> 01:53:35.210
Maria, our abbey is not to be used
as an escape.

01:53:35.483 --> 01:53:37.713
What is it you can't face?

01:53:39.687 --> 01:53:41.120
I can't face him again.

01:53:41.956 --> 01:53:43.480
Him?

01:53:45.059 --> 01:53:47.118
Thank you, Sister Margaretta.

01:53:56.737 --> 01:53:58.364
Captain von Trapp?

01:54:03.811 --> 01:54:06.507
- Are you in love with him?
- I don't know!

01:54:06.747 --> 01:54:08.214
I don't know. I...

01:54:08.749 --> 01:54:12.583
The baroness said I was.
She said that he was in love with me.

01:54:12.853 --> 01:54:15.515
But I didn't want to believe it.

01:54:16.590 --> 01:54:18.888
There were times we looked
at each other.

01:54:19.093 --> 01:54:20.651
I could hardly breathe.

01:54:21.028 --> 01:54:23.724
- Did you let him see your feelings?
- I don't know.

01:54:24.332 --> 01:54:26.994
That's what's torturing me.
I was on God's errand.

01:54:27.201 --> 01:54:32.195
To have asked for his love would have
been wrong. I just couldn't stay.

01:54:34.375 --> 01:54:37.173
I'm ready at this moment
to take my vows.

01:54:38.045 --> 01:54:41.105
- Please help me.
- Maria.

01:54:42.683 --> 01:54:47.382
The love of a man and a woman is holy.
You have a great capacity to love.

01:54:47.621 --> 01:54:50.556
You must find out how God
wants you to spend your love.

01:54:50.858 --> 01:54:54.692
But I pledged my life to God.
I pledged my life to his service.

01:54:54.895 --> 01:54:59.264
My daughter, if you love this man,
it doesn't mean you love God less.

01:55:00.935 --> 01:55:02.800
No.

01:55:03.037 --> 01:55:04.902
You must find out.

01:55:06.640 --> 01:55:09.131
You must go back.

01:55:09.410 --> 01:55:11.378
You can't ask me to do that.

01:55:11.579 --> 01:55:14.070
- Please let me stay. I beg...
- Maria.

01:55:14.281 --> 01:55:18.240
These walls were not built
to shut out problems.

01:55:18.452 --> 01:55:20.044
You have to face them.

01:55:20.621 --> 01:55:23.886
You have to live the life
you were born to live.

01:55:29.764 --> 01:55:34.064
<i>Climb every mountain</i>

01:55:34.301 --> 01:55:38.067
<i>Search high and low</i>

01:55:38.305 --> 01:55:43.072
<i>Follow every byway</i>

01:55:43.310 --> 01:55:47.576
<i>Every path you know</i>

01:55:48.015 --> 01:55:52.475
<i>Climb every mountain</i>

01:55:52.753 --> 01:55:57.087
<i>Ford every stream</i>

01:55:57.324 --> 01:56:01.693
<i>Follow every rainbow</i>

01:56:01.962 --> 01:56:06.296
<i>Till you find your dream</i>

01:56:06.500 --> 01:56:09.594
<i>A dream that will need</i>

01:56:09.837 --> 01:56:14.672
<i>All the love you can give</i>

01:56:15.443 --> 01:56:18.844
<i>Every day of your life</i>

01:56:19.113 --> 01:56:25.518
<i>For as long as you live</i>

01:56:25.820 --> 01:56:30.120
<i>Climb every mountain</i>

01:56:30.357 --> 01:56:34.691
<i>Ford every stream</i>

01:56:34.962 --> 01:56:39.524
<i>Follow every rainbow</i>

01:56:39.733 --> 01:56:48.141
<i>Till you find your dream</i>

01:56:49.243 --> 01:56:52.735
<i>A dream that will need</i>

01:56:53.047 --> 01:56:58.576
<i>All the love you can give</i>

01:56:58.853 --> 01:57:02.345
<i>Every day of your life</i>

01:57:02.590 --> 01:57:09.018
<i>For as long as you live</i>

01:57:09.263 --> 01:57:13.700
<i>Climb every mountain</i>

01:57:13.934 --> 01:57:17.870
<i>Ford every stream</i>

01:57:18.539 --> 01:57:23.169
<i>Follow every rainbow</i>

01:57:23.577 --> 01:57:27.673
<i>Till you find...</i>

01:57:27.915 --> 01:57:37.916
<i>...your dream</i>

01:57:40.461 --> 01:57:44.022
Now, it's not like my children
to be secretive.

01:57:44.265 --> 01:57:46.358
We're not being secretive, Father.

01:57:48.035 --> 01:57:51.368
And it's not like my children
to be late for dinner.

01:57:51.639 --> 01:57:55.075
- We lost track of the time.
- I see.

01:57:55.876 --> 01:57:59.277
Who's going to be the first one
to tell me the truth? Friedrich.

01:57:59.547 --> 01:58:01.606
Brigitta. Liesl.

01:58:02.983 --> 01:58:05.213
Where do you think we were, Father?

01:58:11.792 --> 01:58:15.751
If you don't believe us, you must have
some idea of where you think we were.

01:58:19.333 --> 01:58:21.130
- Marta.
- Yes, Father.

01:58:21.335 --> 01:58:22.597
You tell me.

01:58:23.938 --> 01:58:27.567
Friedrich told you, Father.
We were berry picking.

01:58:28.409 --> 01:58:33.073
- I forgot! You were berry picking.
- Yes, we love berry picking.

01:58:33.314 --> 01:58:34.406
All afternoon?

01:58:34.648 --> 01:58:36.377
- We picked thousands.
- Thousands?

01:58:36.584 --> 01:58:39.485
- They were all over the place.
- What kind of berries?

01:58:39.753 --> 01:58:43.018
- Blueberries, sir.
- Blueberries.

01:58:44.959 --> 01:58:48.326
It's too early for blueberries.

01:58:49.830 --> 01:58:51.923
- They were strawberries.
- Strawberries?

01:58:52.633 --> 01:58:55.329
It's been so cold lately,
they turned blue.

01:59:01.175 --> 01:59:03.336
Very well. Show me the berries.

01:59:04.612 --> 01:59:05.806
- We...
- Well...

01:59:06.046 --> 01:59:08.810
- Show me the berries you picked.
- We don't have them.

01:59:09.049 --> 01:59:11.313
You don't have them?
What happened to them?

01:59:11.552 --> 01:59:14.350
- We...
- We ate them.

01:59:14.555 --> 01:59:17.149
- You ate them?
- Yes!

01:59:17.358 --> 01:59:18.950
- They were so good.
- Delicious.

01:59:19.193 --> 01:59:20.387
Very well.

01:59:20.661 --> 01:59:25.792
Since you've obviously stuffed
yourselves on thousands of berries...

01:59:26.033 --> 01:59:29.969
...you can't be hungry anymore,
so I'll have to tell Frau Schmidt...

01:59:30.204 --> 01:59:33.071
...to skip your dinner.

01:59:42.249 --> 01:59:45.047
It's your fault.
We should have told him the truth.

01:59:45.319 --> 01:59:47.287
And made him boiling mad at us?

01:59:47.488 --> 01:59:49.422
It's better than starving to death.

01:59:49.657 --> 01:59:52.524
We didn't do anything wrong.
We just wanted to see her.

01:59:53.827 --> 01:59:56.921
My stomach's making noises.

01:59:57.364 --> 02:00:00.197
The least they could have done
was to let us say hello.

02:00:01.335 --> 02:00:05.237
- I wonder what grass tastes like.
- I feel awful.

02:00:05.673 --> 02:00:09.939
When Fräulein Maria wanted to feel
better she used to sing that song.

02:00:10.544 --> 02:00:12.011
Let's try it.

02:00:12.246 --> 02:00:14.908
<i>Raindrops on roses</i>

02:00:15.215 --> 02:00:19.242
<i>And whiskers on kittens</i>

02:00:20.087 --> 02:00:22.681
<i>Bright copper kettles</i>

02:00:22.890 --> 02:00:25.950
<i>And warm woolen mittens</i>

02:00:27.294 --> 02:00:33.255
<i>Brown paper packages</i>
<i>Tied up with strings</i>

02:00:33.534 --> 02:00:39.530
<i>These are a few of my favorite things</i>

02:00:39.773 --> 02:00:41.798
Why don't I feel better?

02:00:42.976 --> 02:00:45.274
<i>Girls in white dresses</i>

02:00:45.546 --> 02:00:48.640
<i>With blue satin sashes</i>

02:00:48.916 --> 02:00:54.548
<i>Snowflakes that stay</i>
<i>On my nose and eyelashes</i>

02:00:54.922 --> 02:00:58.085
- <i>Silver white winters...</i>
- Fräulein Maria's back!

02:00:58.292 --> 02:00:59.589
<i>...that melt into springs</i>

02:00:59.993 --> 02:01:03.258
<i>These are a few of my favorite things</i>

02:01:03.497 --> 02:01:06.591
<i>When the dog bites</i>
<i>When the bee stings</i>

02:01:06.800 --> 02:01:08.927
<i>When I'm feeling sad</i>

02:01:09.436 --> 02:01:12.405
<i>I simply remember my favorite things</i>

02:01:12.673 --> 02:01:14.937
<i>And then I don't feel</i>

02:01:15.142 --> 02:01:21.911
<i>So bad</i>

02:01:22.149 --> 02:01:25.175
- Children, I'm so glad to see you.
- We missed you.

02:01:25.419 --> 02:01:26.408
I missed you.

02:01:26.687 --> 02:01:28.814
- Kurt, how are you?
- Hungry.

02:01:30.357 --> 02:01:32.985
- What happened to your finger?
- It got caught.

02:01:33.260 --> 02:01:35.421
- Caught in what?
- Friedrich's teeth.

02:01:36.663 --> 02:01:38.824
- Liesl, you all right?
- Just fair.

02:01:39.032 --> 02:01:42.024
- Any telegrams been delivered lately?
- None at all.

02:01:42.269 --> 02:01:45.705
But I'm learning to accept it.
I'll be glad when school begins.

02:01:46.006 --> 02:01:50.705
Liesl, you can't use school to escape
your problems. You have to face them.

02:01:50.944 --> 02:01:52.377
I have so much to tell you.

02:01:52.646 --> 02:01:54.637
We have things to tell you too.

02:01:54.982 --> 02:01:58.679
The most important thing is
that Father is going to be married.

02:01:58.886 --> 02:01:59.944
Married?

02:02:00.287 --> 02:02:02.312
Yes, to Baroness Schraeder.

02:02:10.230 --> 02:02:11.788
Oh, I see.

02:02:13.634 --> 02:02:17.001
Father, look!
Fräulein Maria's back!

02:02:17.237 --> 02:02:19.296
Fräulein Maria's back from the abbey.

02:02:21.508 --> 02:02:22.566
Good evening, captain.

02:02:24.044 --> 02:02:25.341
Good evening.

02:02:27.881 --> 02:02:29.712
Everyone inside for dinner.

02:02:30.017 --> 02:02:31.575
Dinner!

02:02:40.928 --> 02:02:45.661
You left without saying goodbye.
Even to the children.

02:02:46.667 --> 02:02:48.191
It was wrong of me. Forgive me.

02:02:50.237 --> 02:02:51.397
Why did you?

02:02:51.605 --> 02:02:54.438
Please don't ask me.
The reason no longer exists.

02:02:55.609 --> 02:02:58.703
Fräulein Maria, you've returned.

02:02:59.947 --> 02:03:01.744
Isn't it wonderful, Georg?

02:03:05.052 --> 02:03:07.282
I wish you every happiness,
baroness.

02:03:07.521 --> 02:03:10.217
You too, captain.
The children say you're to marry.

02:03:10.457 --> 02:03:11.583
Thank you, my dear.

02:03:14.127 --> 02:03:17.688
You are back to stay?

02:03:19.766 --> 02:03:23.099
Only until arrangements can be made
for another governess.

02:04:18.792 --> 02:04:20.419
There you are.

02:04:34.808 --> 02:04:37.276
I must speak to cook
about the schnitzel.

02:04:37.544 --> 02:04:40.843
It is entirely too delicious
for my figure.

02:04:41.281 --> 02:04:44.216
And it makes you much too quiet
at the dinner table.

02:04:44.484 --> 02:04:46.475
Or was it the wine?

02:04:46.720 --> 02:04:48.551
Undoubtedly the wine.

02:04:51.124 --> 02:04:53.388
You have no idea
the trouble I'm having...

02:04:53.660 --> 02:04:56.390
...trying to decide on
a wedding present for you.

02:04:56.697 --> 02:04:58.858
Oh, I know. I'm enough.

02:04:59.132 --> 02:05:02.727
But I do want you to have
some little trifle for the occasion.

02:05:02.970 --> 02:05:05.302
At first I thought
of a fountain pen...

02:05:05.539 --> 02:05:07.803
...but you've already got one.

02:05:08.075 --> 02:05:11.010
Then I thought perhaps a villa
in the south of France...

02:05:11.244 --> 02:05:13.906
...but they are so difficult
to gift-wrap.

02:05:14.181 --> 02:05:16.581
Oh, Georg, how do you
feel about yachts?

02:05:16.883 --> 02:05:19.147
A long, sleek one
for the Mediterranean...

02:05:19.386 --> 02:05:22.150
...or a tiny one
for your bathtub, huh?

02:05:24.324 --> 02:05:26.349
- Elsa.
- Where to go on our honeymoon?

02:05:26.593 --> 02:05:28.185
Now, that's a real problem.

02:05:28.395 --> 02:05:31.762
A trip around the world
would be lovely. And then I said:

02:05:32.065 --> 02:05:34.898
"Oh, Elsa, there must be
someplace better to go."

02:05:35.168 --> 02:05:37.602
- But don't worry, darling, I'll...
- Elsa.

02:05:38.271 --> 02:05:39.533
Yes, Georg.

02:05:40.540 --> 02:05:41.871
It's no use...

02:05:43.076 --> 02:05:44.441
...you and I.

02:05:46.013 --> 02:05:49.244
I'm being dishonest to both of us...

02:05:50.584 --> 02:05:52.245
...and utterly unfair to you.

02:05:57.524 --> 02:06:00.254
- When two people talk of marriage...
- No, don't.

02:06:01.128 --> 02:06:03.221
Don't say another word, please.

02:06:06.533 --> 02:06:11.561
You see, there are other things
I've been thinking of.

02:06:12.472 --> 02:06:17.205
Fond as I am of you, I really don't
think you're the right man for me.

02:06:19.746 --> 02:06:22.237
You're much too independent.

02:06:22.549 --> 02:06:27.248
And I need someone
who needs me desperately...

02:06:27.554 --> 02:06:30.546
...or at least needs
my money desperately.

02:06:32.726 --> 02:06:37.629
I've enjoyed every moment we've had
together and I do thank you for that.

02:06:40.400 --> 02:06:42.300
Now, if you'll forgive me...

02:06:42.502 --> 02:06:44.561
...I'll go inside,
pack my little bags...

02:06:44.805 --> 02:06:47.296
...and return to Vienna
where I belong.

02:06:52.679 --> 02:06:54.510
And somewhere out there...

02:06:54.815 --> 02:06:59.184
...is a young lady who, I think...

02:06:59.453 --> 02:07:00.681
...will never be a nun.

02:07:12.833 --> 02:07:15.165
Auf Wiedersehen, darling.

02:07:40.894 --> 02:07:42.054
Hello.

02:07:47.868 --> 02:07:51.463
I thought I just might find you here.

02:07:55.642 --> 02:07:57.906
Was there something you wanted?

02:07:58.345 --> 02:08:01.473
No, no, no. Sit down, please.

02:08:02.415 --> 02:08:03.746
Please.

02:08:08.889 --> 02:08:10.220
May I?

02:08:22.602 --> 02:08:27.335
You know, I was thinking
and I was wondering two things:

02:08:28.508 --> 02:08:32.740
Why did you run away to the abbey?

02:08:33.580 --> 02:08:38.244
And what was it
that made you come back?

02:08:39.920 --> 02:08:44.380
Well, I had an obligation
to fulfill...

02:08:44.591 --> 02:08:46.718
...and I came back to fulfill it.

02:08:47.360 --> 02:08:48.793
Is that all?

02:08:50.130 --> 02:08:52.291
And I missed the children.

02:08:52.632 --> 02:08:53.792
Yes.

02:08:55.068 --> 02:08:57.969
- Only the children?
- No. Yes.

02:08:58.205 --> 02:09:02.039
- Isn't it right that I missed them?
- Oh, yes. Yes, of course.

02:09:02.242 --> 02:09:04.870
I was only hoping that perhaps you...

02:09:05.979 --> 02:09:07.742
Perhaps you might...

02:09:09.482 --> 02:09:10.710
Yes?

02:09:12.485 --> 02:09:17.787
Well, nothing was the same
when you were away...

02:09:18.558 --> 02:09:21.789
...and it'll be all wrong again
after you leave...

02:09:21.995 --> 02:09:26.659
...and I just thought perhaps
you might change your mind.

02:09:30.737 --> 02:09:34.969
Well, I'm sure the baroness will be
able to make things fine for you.

02:09:35.242 --> 02:09:36.573
Maria...

02:09:38.678 --> 02:09:42.170
- There isn't going to be any baroness.
- There isn't?

02:09:44.584 --> 02:09:45.949
No.

02:09:46.253 --> 02:09:48.016
I don't understand.

02:09:50.423 --> 02:09:54.519
Well, we've called off our engagement,
you see, and...

02:09:54.794 --> 02:09:58.252
- Oh, I'm sorry.
- Yes. You are?

02:09:59.432 --> 02:10:01.525
- You did?
- Yes.

02:10:02.669 --> 02:10:07.197
Well, you can't marry someone
when you're...

02:10:09.776 --> 02:10:11.835
...in love with someone else...

02:10:15.215 --> 02:10:16.648
...can you?

02:10:51.518 --> 02:10:53.816
The Reverend Mother always says:

02:10:54.054 --> 02:10:57.490
"When the Lord closes a door,
somewhere He opens a window."

02:11:05.899 --> 02:11:08.925
What else does
the Reverend Mother say?

02:11:09.869 --> 02:11:12.269
That you have to look for your life.

02:11:13.940 --> 02:11:16.500
Is that why you came back?

02:11:20.547 --> 02:11:22.014
And have you found it...

02:11:23.016 --> 02:11:24.176
...Maria?

02:11:25.952 --> 02:11:27.943
I think I have.

02:11:30.690 --> 02:11:32.089
I know I have.

02:11:34.594 --> 02:11:36.255
I love you.

02:11:40.233 --> 02:11:42.098
Oh, can this be happening to me?

02:11:45.472 --> 02:11:50.876
<i>Perhaps I had a wicked childhood</i>

02:11:52.379 --> 02:11:57.612
<i>Perhaps I had a miserable youth</i>

02:11:59.486 --> 02:12:05.425
<i>But somewhere</i>
<i>In my wicked, miserable past</i>

02:12:05.925 --> 02:12:11.727
<i>There must have been a moment of truth</i>

02:12:12.665 --> 02:12:19.434
<i>For here you are</i>
<i>Standing there loving me</i>

02:12:20.173 --> 02:12:26.169
<i>Whether or not you should</i>

02:12:26.813 --> 02:12:33.616
<i>So somewhere in my youth or childhood</i>

02:12:34.487 --> 02:12:42.121
<i>I must have done something good</i>

02:12:43.363 --> 02:12:46.332
<i>Nothing comes from nothing</i>

02:12:47.467 --> 02:12:51.335
<i>Nothing ever could</i>

02:12:52.172 --> 02:13:01.046
<i>So somewhere in my youth or childhood</i>

02:13:02.615 --> 02:13:12.115
<i>I must have done something good</i>

02:13:12.992 --> 02:13:17.827
Do you know when I first
started loving you?

02:13:18.231 --> 02:13:22.133
That night at dinner, when you sat
on that ridiculous pine cone.

02:13:22.368 --> 02:13:23.665
What?

02:13:25.004 --> 02:13:28.462
I knew the first time you blew
that silly whistle.

02:13:29.375 --> 02:13:31.366
Oh, my love.

02:13:35.148 --> 02:13:43.055
<i>For here you are</i>
<i>Standing there loving me</i>

02:13:45.024 --> 02:13:50.860
<i>Whether or not you should</i>

02:13:52.232 --> 02:13:59.263
<i>So somewhere in my youth or childhood</i>

02:14:00.073 --> 02:14:07.775
<i>I must have done something good</i>

02:14:08.948 --> 02:14:12.440
<i>Nothing comes from nothing</i>

02:14:13.186 --> 02:14:16.212
<i>Nothing ever could</i>

02:14:16.456 --> 02:14:22.258
<i>So somewhere in my youth...</i>

02:14:22.529 --> 02:14:24.759
<i>...or childhood</i>

02:14:27.867 --> 02:14:34.397
<i>I must have done something</i>

02:14:36.442 --> 02:14:49.082
<i>Something good</i>

02:14:55.795 --> 02:14:57.319
Maria.

02:14:59.165 --> 02:15:03.761
Is there anyone I should go to,
to ask permission to marry you?

02:15:07.674 --> 02:15:10.234
- Why don't we ask...
- The children?

02:16:58.751 --> 02:17:02.778
<i>How do you solve a problem like Maria?</i>

02:17:03.589 --> 02:17:07.286
<i>How do you catch a cloud</i>
<i>And pin it down?</i>

02:17:08.261 --> 02:17:12.425
<i>How do you find a word</i>
<i>That means Maria?</i>

02:17:12.865 --> 02:17:13.854
<i>A flibbertigibbet</i>

02:17:14.100 --> 02:17:17.365
<i>A will-o'-the-wisp</i>
<i>A clown</i>

02:17:17.570 --> 02:17:22.132
<i>Many a thing you know</i>
<i>You'd like to tell her</i>

02:17:22.575 --> 02:17:26.602
<i>Many a thing she ought to understand</i>

02:17:27.313 --> 02:17:31.613
<i>But how do you make her stay</i>
<i>And listen to all you say?</i>

02:17:31.984 --> 02:17:35.920
<i>How do you keep a wave upon the sand?</i>

02:17:36.255 --> 02:17:41.249
<i>Oh, how do you solve</i>
<i>A problem like Maria?</i>

02:17:41.627 --> 02:17:48.260
<i>How do you hold a moonbeam</i>
<i>In your hand?</i>

02:19:54.360 --> 02:19:55.918
Herr Detweiler!

02:19:58.531 --> 02:20:01.193
- Heil Hitler.
- Oh, good afternoon, Herr Zeller.

02:20:01.434 --> 02:20:04.733
Perhaps you've not heard.
I am now the Gauleiter.

02:20:05.037 --> 02:20:06.561
Heil Hitler.

02:20:07.473 --> 02:20:08.633
Heil Hitler.

02:20:08.941 --> 02:20:11.205
I've come from
Captain von Trapp's house.

02:20:11.644 --> 02:20:15.239
The only one in the area
not flying the Third Reich flag...

02:20:15.481 --> 02:20:16.743
...since the Anschluss.

02:20:16.949 --> 02:20:19.110
- But we have dealt with that.
- I don't...

02:20:19.385 --> 02:20:22.320
The housekeeper told me
that I would find you here.

02:20:22.588 --> 02:20:24.283
The only thing she'd tell me.

02:20:24.790 --> 02:20:27.315
What kind of information
are you looking for?

02:20:27.593 --> 02:20:29.458
When will the captain return?

02:20:29.996 --> 02:20:33.932
Well, he's on his honeymoon trip.
He's not been in touch with us.

02:20:34.166 --> 02:20:39.001
Am I to believe he hasn't communicated
with his children in over a month?

02:20:39.272 --> 02:20:41.172
How many men do you know...

02:20:41.440 --> 02:20:44.739
...who communicate with their children
while honeymooning?

02:20:45.645 --> 02:20:49.342
Upon his return, he'll fill
his proper position in the new order.

02:20:49.649 --> 02:20:52.015
Naturally.
And may I congratulate you...

02:20:52.251 --> 02:20:56.915
...and your people in allowing the
festival to go on tonight as planned.

02:20:57.456 --> 02:21:00.914
Why should it not go on?
Nothing in Austria has changed.

02:21:01.160 --> 02:21:04.561
Singing and music will
show this to the world.

02:21:04.764 --> 02:21:06.459
Austria is the same.

02:21:07.333 --> 02:21:08.698
Heil Hitler.

02:21:10.870 --> 02:21:12.462
Heil Hitler.

02:21:14.140 --> 02:21:15.368
Come, let's go home.

02:21:15.608 --> 02:21:19.100
- Why was he so cross?
- Everybody's cross these days.

02:21:19.312 --> 02:21:22.679
Maybe the flag with the black spider
makes people nervous.

02:21:22.882 --> 02:21:25.817
- Will Father be in trouble?
- He doesn't have to be.

02:21:26.052 --> 02:21:28.782
The thing to do
is to get along with everybody.

02:21:29.021 --> 02:21:31.216
Remember that tonight at the concert.

02:21:31.457 --> 02:21:34.358
Are we really going to sing
before a lot of people?

02:21:34.560 --> 02:21:36.653
Look. The von Trapp Family Singers:

02:21:36.862 --> 02:21:41.458
Liesl, Friedrich, Louisa, Brigitta,
Kurt, Marta and Gretl.

02:21:41.667 --> 02:21:46.036
- Why am I always last?
- Because you are the most important.

02:21:46.739 --> 02:21:48.366
There we go.

02:21:54.246 --> 02:21:57.704
Are you sure Father will approve
of our singing in public?

02:21:57.917 --> 02:22:00.215
He'll be pleased and proud.

02:22:00.686 --> 02:22:03.154
- Liesl, do you think so?
- Don't you trust me?

02:22:03.356 --> 02:22:04.380
No.

02:22:04.590 --> 02:22:06.683
You're a very intelligent girl.

02:22:07.226 --> 02:22:09.387
Liesl. Liesl!

02:22:10.329 --> 02:22:11.523
Rolfe!

02:22:12.531 --> 02:22:14.556
I'm so glad to see you.
It's been su...

02:22:14.767 --> 02:22:15.859
Good afternoon.

02:22:16.268 --> 02:22:19.203
Give this to your father
as soon as he's home.

02:22:19.872 --> 02:22:21.737
- He's on his honeymoon.
- I know.

02:22:21.941 --> 02:22:25.274
- You do?
- We make it our business to know all.

02:22:26.012 --> 02:22:28.572
- Who's "we"?
- See that he gets it.

02:22:28.781 --> 02:22:31.113
- What is it?
- It's a telegram from Berlin.

02:22:31.951 --> 02:22:34.442
Don't you want to deliver it yourself?

02:22:34.920 --> 02:22:37.548
I'm occupied
with more important matters.

02:22:37.757 --> 02:22:40.248
And your father had better be too.

02:22:40.526 --> 02:22:42.016
But, Rolfe!

02:23:05.117 --> 02:23:06.778
Father!

02:23:07.053 --> 02:23:09.715
- We didn't expect you so soon.
- Hello, hello!

02:23:09.955 --> 02:23:12.753
We didn't expect you home
until next week!

02:23:12.958 --> 02:23:18.396
- Did you bring souvenirs from Paris?
- Hello! How are you?

02:23:19.498 --> 02:23:20.795
Why didn't you call us?

02:23:21.000 --> 02:23:22.934
We couldn't get through.

02:23:23.235 --> 02:23:25.169
I had nothing to do with that.

02:23:25.438 --> 02:23:27.463
We came back as fast as we could.

02:23:27.773 --> 02:23:29.934
Well, well, well! We missed you!

02:23:30.176 --> 02:23:32.610
- We missed you!
- We missed kissing you.

02:23:32.812 --> 02:23:35.645
We missed all the noise
in the morning.

02:23:35.915 --> 02:23:40.113
- Mostly, we missed hearing you sing.
- Oh, you came back just in time.

02:23:40.319 --> 02:23:42.082
Look, Fräulein Maria...

02:23:42.288 --> 02:23:43.915
I mean Mother.

02:23:44.323 --> 02:23:46.814
We're going to sing
in the festival tonight.

02:23:47.026 --> 02:23:49.153
We've been having a lovely time!

02:23:49.428 --> 02:23:51.487
We've been rehearsing all...

02:23:52.998 --> 02:23:55.330
Surprise! Surprise!

02:23:56.001 --> 02:23:58.492
Surprises for you on the terrace.

02:24:01.540 --> 02:24:02.939
We'll talk about this.

02:24:03.142 --> 02:24:07.442
I would've told you but you were away.
I had to make a last-minute decision.

02:24:07.713 --> 02:24:10.204
I was fortunate to enter them at all.

02:24:10.449 --> 02:24:15.182
They'll be the talk of the festival.
Imagine, seven children in one family!

02:24:15.387 --> 02:24:17.014
Max!

02:24:17.623 --> 02:24:20.456
Somehow I recall having made it
quite clear to you...

02:24:20.726 --> 02:24:23.388
...how I feel about my family
singing in public!

02:24:23.662 --> 02:24:25.357
The committee was enchanted.

02:24:25.564 --> 02:24:28.727
- What did they say?
- I have never heard such enthusiasm.

02:24:29.001 --> 02:24:33.301
- Don't you think just this once...?
- Absolutely out of the question.

02:24:33.539 --> 02:24:37.669
- Georg, this is for Austria.
- For Austria?

02:24:38.043 --> 02:24:41.308
- There is no Austria!
- But the Anschluss was peaceful.

02:24:41.547 --> 02:24:45.005
- Let's at least be grateful for that.
- Grateful?

02:24:46.886 --> 02:24:48.547
You know, Max...

02:24:49.421 --> 02:24:52.686
...sometimes I don't believe
I know you.

02:24:55.361 --> 02:24:56.726
Father, I forgot.

02:24:57.563 --> 02:24:59.155
This is for you.

02:25:08.941 --> 02:25:12.934
Maria, he has got to at least pretend
to work with these people.

02:25:13.212 --> 02:25:14.736
You must convince him.

02:25:14.947 --> 02:25:17.711
Max, I can't ask him
to be less than he is.

02:25:17.950 --> 02:25:21.249
Then I'll talk to him.
If the children don't sing, well...

02:25:21.520 --> 02:25:23.750
...it will be a reflection
on Austria.

02:25:24.557 --> 02:25:27.924
Oh, I know.
It wouldn't do me any good either.

02:25:33.098 --> 02:25:35.760
Mother? That sounds so nice.

02:25:36.035 --> 02:25:38.765
- I like calling you "Mother."
- I like hearing it.

02:25:38.971 --> 02:25:42.702
You love Father very much.
I can tell you do.

02:25:42.908 --> 02:25:43.704
Very much.

02:25:43.976 --> 02:25:47.275
Mother, what do you do when you
think you love someone?

02:25:47.980 --> 02:25:53.282
I mean, when you stop loving someone
or he stops loving you?

02:25:55.888 --> 02:25:57.947
Well, you cry a little.

02:25:58.390 --> 02:26:00.483
Then you wait for the sun to come out.

02:26:00.793 --> 02:26:02.124
It always does.

02:26:02.394 --> 02:26:05.955
There are so many things I think
I should know but I don't.

02:26:06.165 --> 02:26:08.133
- I really don't.
- How can you?

02:26:08.400 --> 02:26:10.595
Sometimes I feel the world is ending.

02:26:10.836 --> 02:26:14.067
- Then you feel it's just beginning?
- Yes!

02:26:14.273 --> 02:26:18.505
It was that way with me. And for you
it will be just as wonderful.

02:26:19.178 --> 02:26:21.078
Do you really think so?

02:26:21.981 --> 02:26:25.917
<i>When you're 16 going on 17</i>

02:26:26.185 --> 02:26:29.780
<i>Waiting for life to start</i>

02:26:30.456 --> 02:26:34.290
<i>Somebody kind</i>
<i>Who touches your mind</i>

02:26:34.526 --> 02:26:38.826
<i>Will suddenly touch your heart</i>

02:26:39.265 --> 02:26:40.960
<i>When that happens</i>

02:26:41.433 --> 02:26:43.367
<i>After it happens</i>

02:26:43.602 --> 02:26:47.470
<i>Nothing is quite the same</i>

02:26:47.706 --> 02:26:49.264
<i>Somehow I know</i>

02:26:49.541 --> 02:26:51.668
<i>I'll jump up and go</i>

02:26:51.877 --> 02:26:56.177
<i>If ever he calls my name</i>

02:26:56.448 --> 02:27:00.350
<i>Gone are your old ideas of life</i>

02:27:00.619 --> 02:27:04.817
<i>The old ideas grow dim</i>

02:27:05.057 --> 02:27:09.460
<i>Lo and behold</i>
<i>You're someone's wife</i>

02:27:10.396 --> 02:27:16.392
<i>And you belong to him</i>

02:27:16.702 --> 02:27:21.002
<i>You may think this kind of adventure</i>

02:27:21.206 --> 02:27:25.074
<i>Never may come to you</i>

02:27:26.178 --> 02:27:31.548
<i>Darling, 16 going on 17</i>

02:27:32.384 --> 02:27:36.514
<i>Wait a year...</i>

02:27:37.323 --> 02:27:42.556
<i>- I'll wait a year</i>
<i>...or two</i>

02:27:42.995 --> 02:27:50.333
<i>Just wait a year...</i>

02:27:51.203 --> 02:27:59.838
<i>...or two</i>

02:28:02.247 --> 02:28:03.839
Liesl.

02:28:20.299 --> 02:28:21.630
What is it?

02:28:22.568 --> 02:28:23.933
Berlin.

02:28:24.403 --> 02:28:26.268
They've offered me a commission.

02:28:26.538 --> 02:28:29.063
I've been requested
to accept immediately...

02:28:29.308 --> 02:28:33.301
...and report to their naval base
at Bremerhaven tomorrow.

02:28:33.912 --> 02:28:37.905
I knew this would happen.
I didn't think it would be so soon.

02:28:38.150 --> 02:28:41.642
To refuse them would be fatal
for all of us.

02:28:42.888 --> 02:28:46.654
And joining them would be unthinkable.

02:28:52.831 --> 02:28:54.594
Get the children all together.

02:28:54.933 --> 02:28:58.130
Don't say anything to worry them.
Just get them ready.

02:28:59.104 --> 02:29:01.470
We've got to get out of Austria...

02:29:03.142 --> 02:29:04.803
...and this house...

02:29:07.146 --> 02:29:08.579
...tonight.

02:29:52.491 --> 02:29:54.891
This strains my back
and breaks my heart...

02:29:55.160 --> 02:29:57.993
...when I think of the children
missing the festival.

02:29:58.297 --> 02:30:00.959
By your announcement
we'll be over the border.

02:30:01.200 --> 02:30:03.634
Do you appreciate
the sacrifice I'm making?

02:30:03.836 --> 02:30:05.133
You have no choice.

02:30:05.370 --> 02:30:08.203
I know. That's why I'm making it.

02:30:08.907 --> 02:30:11.034
Why doesn't Father turn the motor on?

02:30:11.243 --> 02:30:14.679
Because he doesn't want anyone
to hear us.

02:30:18.317 --> 02:30:20.751
What will Frau Schmidt and Franz say?

02:30:21.019 --> 02:30:24.546
They'll be able to answer honestly
they didn't know anything.

02:30:24.756 --> 02:30:28.988
- Will we be coming back here?
- Someday, Liesl. I do hope someday.

02:30:29.228 --> 02:30:34.165
Are Father and Uncle Max going to push
the car all the way to Switzerland?

02:31:00.959 --> 02:31:03.359
Something wrong
with your car, captain?

02:31:03.695 --> 02:31:05.959
Yes, we couldn't get it started.

02:31:09.735 --> 02:31:10.963
Karl.

02:31:12.938 --> 02:31:16.430
Fix Captain von Trapp's car
so that it will start.

02:31:39.631 --> 02:31:41.428
Excellent, Karl.

02:31:44.803 --> 02:31:47.966
I've not asked you where you
and your family are going.

02:31:48.473 --> 02:31:50.600
Nor have you asked me why I'm here.

02:31:50.809 --> 02:31:54.575
Apparently we both suffer
from a deplorable lack of curiosity.

02:31:55.447 --> 02:31:57.915
You never answered the telegram...

02:31:58.150 --> 02:32:01.449
...from the Admiral of the Navy
of the Third Reich.

02:32:01.687 --> 02:32:04.155
I was under the impression,
Herr Zeller...

02:32:04.423 --> 02:32:07.915
...that the contents of telegrams
in Austria are private!

02:32:08.627 --> 02:32:12.154
At least, the Austria I know.

02:32:13.298 --> 02:32:14.925
I have my orders...

02:32:15.167 --> 02:32:17.328
...to take you
to Bremerhaven tonight...

02:32:17.603 --> 02:32:19.798
...where you will accept
your commission.

02:32:20.939 --> 02:32:26.377
I'm afraid that's going to be
quite impossible.

02:32:26.979 --> 02:32:28.708
You see, we...

02:32:29.281 --> 02:32:32.114
...all of us, the entire family,
will be...

02:32:33.185 --> 02:32:35.210
...singing in the festival tonight.

02:32:35.520 --> 02:32:37.988
As a matter of fact, we're going now.

02:32:38.624 --> 02:32:41.491
We couldn't possibly
let them down now.

02:32:41.693 --> 02:32:44.662
- I just hope we're not too late.
- Yes.

02:32:44.896 --> 02:32:47.797
You ask me to believe that you,
Captain von Trapp...

02:32:48.033 --> 02:32:49.500
...are singing in a concert?

02:32:49.901 --> 02:32:54.031
Believe me, it will be a performance
beyond anything even I've dreamt of.

02:32:54.406 --> 02:32:59.036
Like you, Herr Zeller,
I, too, am a man of hidden talents.

02:32:59.745 --> 02:33:01.076
Yes.

02:33:01.346 --> 02:33:03.837
Here, program.

02:33:08.854 --> 02:33:11.186
It says only the names
of the children.

02:33:11.423 --> 02:33:14.688
It says
the von Trapp Family Singers...

02:33:14.926 --> 02:33:17.986
...and I am the head of
the von Trapp family, am I not?

02:33:20.265 --> 02:33:24.065
And these travel clothes
that you're all wearing?

02:33:24.903 --> 02:33:26.427
Our costumes, naturally.

02:33:26.705 --> 02:33:30.106
This night air is not good
for the children's voices.

02:33:36.348 --> 02:33:39.875
Well, a slight delay in my orders
will not be serious.

02:33:41.086 --> 02:33:42.610
Therefore...

02:33:43.455 --> 02:33:45.082
...you will sing.

02:33:46.024 --> 02:33:48.015
You will all sing.

02:33:48.393 --> 02:33:50.918
But only because that's what I want.

02:33:51.863 --> 02:33:55.299
It will demonstrate that nothing
in Austria has changed.

02:33:56.034 --> 02:33:58.229
And when you have finished singing...

02:33:58.537 --> 02:34:01.700
...you, Captain von Trapp, will be
taken to Bremerhaven.

02:34:02.974 --> 02:34:05.704
Now, if you will all get
into your car...

02:34:05.944 --> 02:34:09.778
...we will escort the von Trapp Family
Singers to the festival.

02:34:10.649 --> 02:34:12.810
No escort will be necessary.

02:34:13.051 --> 02:34:15.542
Necessary? A pleasure, captain.

02:34:16.455 --> 02:34:20.323
After all, we would not want you
to get lost in the crowds.

02:34:21.560 --> 02:34:23.050
Would we?

02:34:23.729 --> 02:34:24.889
No.

02:34:41.113 --> 02:34:44.276
<i>Sew, a needle pulling thread</i>

02:34:44.483 --> 02:34:47.680
<i>La, a note to follow sew</i>

02:34:47.953 --> 02:34:51.411
<i>Tea, a drink with jam and bread</i>

02:34:51.623 --> 02:34:55.423
<i>A drink with jam and bread</i>

02:35:05.003 --> 02:35:07.164
<i>Tea with jam</i>
<i>Jam and bread</i>

02:35:13.044 --> 02:35:16.377
<i>- With jam</i>
<i>- A, B, C</i>

02:35:16.615 --> 02:35:19.846
<i>- With jam</i>
<i>- Do-re-mi</i>

02:35:20.051 --> 02:35:23.646
<i>Tea with jam and bread</i>

02:35:23.889 --> 02:35:25.220
<i>With jam and bread</i>

02:35:25.490 --> 02:35:27.014
<i>With jam</i>
<i>With jam...</i>

02:35:27.225 --> 02:35:36.031
<i>...and bread</i>

02:35:58.023 --> 02:36:01.151
My fellow Austrians...

02:36:02.427 --> 02:36:06.989
...I shall not be seeing you again,
perhaps for a very long time.

02:36:08.400 --> 02:36:10.061
I would like to sing for you now...

02:36:11.670 --> 02:36:13.228
...a love song.

02:36:15.207 --> 02:36:17.402
I know you share this love.

02:36:18.710 --> 02:36:22.407
I pray that you will never let it die.

02:36:35.193 --> 02:36:38.720
<i>Edelweiss</i>

02:36:38.930 --> 02:36:42.127
<i>Edelweiss</i>

02:36:42.400 --> 02:36:48.134
<i>Every morning you greet me</i>

02:36:48.540 --> 02:36:51.600
<i>Small and white</i>

02:36:51.877 --> 02:36:54.641
<i>Clean and bright</i>

02:36:55.213 --> 02:37:00.310
<i>You look happy to meet me</i>

02:37:01.086 --> 02:37:03.111
<i>Blossom of snow</i>

02:37:03.388 --> 02:37:06.983
<i>May you bloom and grow</i>

02:37:07.225 --> 02:37:12.891
<i>Bloom and grow forever</i>

02:37:14.399 --> 02:37:16.890
<i>Edelweiss</i>

02:37:17.135 --> 02:37:19.763
<i>Edelweiss</i>

02:37:19.971 --> 02:37:25.967
<i>Bless my homeland forever</i>

02:37:30.482 --> 02:37:33.576
<i>Edelweiss</i>

02:37:33.818 --> 02:37:35.149
<i>Edel...</i>

02:37:42.527 --> 02:37:45.621
<i>Small and white</i>

02:37:45.830 --> 02:37:48.697
<i>Clean and bright</i>

02:37:48.934 --> 02:37:54.270
<i>You look happy to meet me</i>

02:37:55.106 --> 02:37:57.074
<i>Blossom of snow</i>

02:37:57.275 --> 02:38:00.676
<i>May you bloom and grow</i>

02:38:01.346 --> 02:38:07.342
<i>Bloom and grow forever</i>

02:38:07.819 --> 02:38:10.720
<i>Edelweiss</i>

02:38:11.022 --> 02:38:13.786
<i>Edelweiss</i>

02:38:14.392 --> 02:38:22.629
<i>Bless my homeland forever</i>

02:38:40.352 --> 02:38:41.910
I think it'll work.

02:38:42.654 --> 02:38:44.417
I shall miss all of you.

02:38:44.923 --> 02:38:47.357
I shall miss the money
I could have made with you.

02:38:50.762 --> 02:38:52.320
Thank you, ladies and gentlemen.

02:38:53.064 --> 02:38:55.726
The competition has come
to its conclusion...

02:38:56.001 --> 02:38:59.095
...except, we don't know
yet what that conclusion will be.

02:39:00.071 --> 02:39:02.596
And while the judges
arrive at their decision...

02:39:02.874 --> 02:39:05.900
...I have been given permission
to offer you an encore.

02:39:06.177 --> 02:39:09.374
This will be the last opportunity
the von Trapps will have...

02:39:09.614 --> 02:39:12.014
...of singing together
for a long, long time.

02:39:13.084 --> 02:39:17.077
Even now, officials are waiting
in this auditorium...

02:39:17.355 --> 02:39:20.085
...to escort Captain von Trapp
to his new command...

02:39:20.291 --> 02:39:23.852
...in the naval forces
of the Third Reich.

02:39:28.533 --> 02:39:33.061
And so, ladies and gentlemen,
the family von Trapp again...

02:39:33.705 --> 02:39:35.969
...to bid you farewell.

02:39:43.214 --> 02:39:46.809
<i>There's a sad sort of clanging</i>
<i>From the clock in the hall</i>

02:39:47.085 --> 02:39:50.418
<i>And the bells in the steeple too</i>

02:39:50.922 --> 02:39:54.790
<i>And up in the nursery</i>
<i>An absurd little bird</i>

02:39:54.993 --> 02:39:57.427
<i>Is popping out to say "coo-coo"</i>

02:39:57.629 --> 02:39:59.290
<i>Coo-coo</i>

02:39:59.564 --> 02:40:00.553
<i>Coo-coo</i>

02:40:00.832 --> 02:40:02.424
<i>Regretfully they tell us</i>

02:40:02.634 --> 02:40:04.431
<i>But firmly they compel us</i>

02:40:04.669 --> 02:40:07.433
<i>To say goodbye</i>

02:40:07.639 --> 02:40:12.804
<i>To you</i>

02:40:15.780 --> 02:40:19.307
<i>So long, farewell</i>
<i>Auf Wiedersehen, good night</i>

02:40:19.584 --> 02:40:23.315
<i>We hate to go</i>
<i>And miss this pretty sight</i>

02:40:29.494 --> 02:40:33.089
<i>So long, farewell</i>
<i>Auf Wiedersehen, adieu</i>

02:40:33.298 --> 02:40:36.961
<i>Adieu, adieu</i>
<i>To you and you and you</i>

02:40:43.274 --> 02:40:46.869
<i>So long, farewell</i>
<i>Auf Wiedersehen, goodbye</i>

02:40:47.112 --> 02:40:48.704
<i>We flit, we float</i>

02:40:48.980 --> 02:40:50.641
<i>We fleetly flee, we fly</i>

02:40:57.021 --> 02:41:00.821
<i>So long, farewell</i>
<i>Auf Wiedersehen, goodbye</i>

02:41:01.025 --> 02:41:04.392
<i>The sun has gone to bed</i>
<i>And so must I</i>

02:41:04.662 --> 02:41:08.462
<i>Goodbye</i>

02:41:08.700 --> 02:41:14.400
<i>Goodbye</i>

02:41:14.639 --> 02:41:19.838
<i>Goodbye</i>

02:41:20.078 --> 02:41:27.246
<i>Goodbye</i>

02:41:59.050 --> 02:42:03.180
Ladies and gentlemen, I have here the
decision of our distinguished judges.

02:42:03.388 --> 02:42:05.948
We will start with the award
for third prize.

02:42:06.591 --> 02:42:08.923
For this honor,
the judges have named...

02:42:09.194 --> 02:42:13.790
...the first soloist of the choir
of St. Agatha's Church in Murback.

02:42:14.065 --> 02:42:16.295
Fräulein Schweiger.

02:42:53.238 --> 02:42:57.174
Second prize
to The Toby Reiser Quintet.

02:43:25.136 --> 02:43:29.300
And the first prize,
the highest honor in all Austria...

02:43:29.540 --> 02:43:32.634
...the von Trapp Family Singers.

02:43:45.023 --> 02:43:46.684
The family von Trapp.

02:44:01.306 --> 02:44:02.364
They're gone!

02:44:21.059 --> 02:44:22.492
Come with me.

02:44:26.331 --> 02:44:28.322
Quickly, quickly.

02:44:29.233 --> 02:44:31.428
I have a place you can hide.

02:44:32.170 --> 02:44:35.435
Slowly, slowly.

02:44:46.417 --> 02:44:48.112
Open this gate.

02:44:49.253 --> 02:44:50.845
Good evening.

02:44:53.358 --> 02:44:54.791
Hurry up, woman.

02:45:14.645 --> 02:45:15.907
Two men in there.

02:45:16.114 --> 02:45:17.979
Six of you cover the yard.

02:45:18.216 --> 02:45:20.446
You two, cover the corridor.

02:45:34.932 --> 02:45:38.493
Reverend Mother, we didn't realize
we put the abbey in this danger.

02:45:38.770 --> 02:45:41.295
No, Maria, it was right for you
to come here.

02:45:41.506 --> 02:45:43.406
We thought we might borrow
your car.

02:45:43.608 --> 02:45:45.508
I'm afraid our car will do you
no good now.

02:45:46.110 --> 02:45:47.771
I've been listening to the wires.

02:45:47.979 --> 02:45:50.504
The borders have just been closed.

02:45:56.354 --> 02:45:58.652
All right,
if the borders are closed...

02:45:59.957 --> 02:46:03.256
...then we'll drive up into the hills
and go over the mountains on foot.

02:46:03.861 --> 02:46:05.852
- The children...
- We'll help them.

02:46:06.130 --> 02:46:08.291
We can do it without help, Father.

02:46:09.333 --> 02:46:10.698
Maria.

02:46:11.436 --> 02:46:14.030
You will not be alone.
Remember:

02:46:14.272 --> 02:46:17.366
"I will lift up mine eyes unto
the hills from whence cometh my help."

02:46:18.342 --> 02:46:19.434
Yes, Mother.

02:46:20.812 --> 02:46:22.973
- I'm scared.
- Me too.

02:46:35.059 --> 02:46:36.219
God be with you.

02:46:43.167 --> 02:46:44.725
- Mother.
- Yes?

02:46:44.969 --> 02:46:48.166
Would it help if we sang
about our favorite things?

02:46:48.406 --> 02:46:51.398
No, darling.
This is one time it would not help.

02:46:51.676 --> 02:46:54.873
You must be very quiet.
Hold tight to me.

02:49:09.547 --> 02:49:10.775
Let's try the roof.

02:50:07.038 --> 02:50:09.268
Rolfe, please.

02:50:14.378 --> 02:50:15.868
No, wait.

02:50:25.690 --> 02:50:27.021
Maria.

02:50:28.092 --> 02:50:29.525
Children.

02:50:33.564 --> 02:50:36.590
It's you we want, not them.

02:50:36.967 --> 02:50:38.696
Put that down.

02:50:39.770 --> 02:50:43.069
Not another move,
or I'll shoot.

02:50:44.775 --> 02:50:46.800
You're only a boy.

02:50:49.814 --> 02:50:53.477
- You don't really belong to them.
- Stay where you are.

02:50:55.252 --> 02:50:57.243
Come away with us.

02:50:58.489 --> 02:50:59.649
Before it's too late.

02:51:00.257 --> 02:51:02.589
Not another step.
I'll kill you.

02:51:04.895 --> 02:51:08.228
- You give that to me, Rolfe.
- Did you hear me?

02:51:09.233 --> 02:51:10.791
I'll kill you.

02:51:12.670 --> 02:51:14.137
Rolfe.

02:51:32.523 --> 02:51:33.854
You'll never be one of them.

02:51:36.627 --> 02:51:38.322
Lieutenant!

02:51:38.596 --> 02:51:39.722
They're here!

02:51:39.930 --> 02:51:41.488
They're here, lieutenant!

02:52:22.807 --> 02:52:24.468
Reverend Mother.

02:52:25.743 --> 02:52:27.574
I have sinned.

02:52:28.746 --> 02:52:30.907
I too, Reverend Mother.

02:52:32.550 --> 02:52:34.882
What is this sin, my children?

02:53:40.165 --> 02:54:10.154
